{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom","id":1515686,"title":"Safety vs. Freedom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-20T13:15:28-07:00","id":1515686,"title":"Safety vs. Freedom","content":"<br /> The main reason the Technocracy use to control the world and the Consensus, is safety. Supposedly, they have changed the world from hell on earth, where femons and dragons flew around killing ppl and spirits were everywhere eating children, into WoD modern times, where you can be shot, exploded or even mauled by a freaking wolf-man, but hey, at least there are no umbrood flying around. <br /> Now, in DA, there were no paradox, there were no strict control over consensus, but there was already a Gauntlet (as always did). Here is the rating of the Gauntlet in DA<br /> <br /> <img width=\"402\" height=\"243\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/H20QfJX/Smart-Select-20230618-183218-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/H20QfJX/Smart-Select-20230618-183218-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/H20QfJX/Smart-Select-20230618-183218-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> A private home has a rating of 6. And a marketplace has 8.<br /> Now, this is the Gauntlet in a time where Paradox is a thing and the Tecnocracy has control over the Consensus:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"398\" height=\"425\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/yRk7GJh/Smart-Select-20230620-153338-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/yRk7GJh/Smart-Select-20230620-153338-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/yRk7GJh/Smart-Select-20230620-153338-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Downtown has a rating of 8. Which is the same as a busy market place in DA.<br /> So, after all the work of the Technocracy, all the deviants being hunted and killed, all the effort to remove anything mystical from Reality, all that changed was +1 in rating in Gauntlet?<br /> <br /> So, is this safety thing only Technocratic propaganda, since the Gauntlet is not much stronger than it was in DA, or are the Gauntlet rating just the authors screw up?<br /> <br /> Also, regarding this freedom vs. safety topic between Trads and Crats. How much of freedom should the Traditions aim in a possible new golden age future?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T15:53:18-07:00","id":1515699,"title":"","content":"Thank the Technocracy that there's a lot more downtown now and a lot less deep wilderness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T18:23:46-07:00","id":1515708,"title":"","content":"Safety is a bit short. Stability, progress on many tracks, and access are more the premises that the Technocracy keep their appeal on.<br /> <br /> As a point of comparison, the notion of a gun is certainly a way of ensuring safety, but part of that is because a gun will work for you no matter who you are, what your mindset, destiny, disposition, morality, etc. While the technologies that the Technocracy chases can get arcane and require specialization, the Technocracy's inevitable aim is that the principles that all the technologies work at are technically accessible to the lay person. The Time Table is also a general principle that keeps the Technocracy rolling out new technologies that better address standing problems in it's more unified world, and with that a new norm that sees the masses keeping pace with that roll out. This isn't a strictly &quot;for the people&quot; take, simply that it's easier to have advanced technologies when your baselines are easy to use and grasp. For as totalitarian and imperialistic as the Technocracy is, that rooting of the power in the paradigm into what the unAwakened can personally handle did them a lot of wonders for controlling the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T17:35:13-07:00","id":1515809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515699#post1515699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank the Technocracy that there's a lot more downtown now and a lot less deep wilderness.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is not necessarily thanls to technocracy. It's due to the increase in world population. This could happen in a Trad consenuss scenario as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515708#post1515708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safety is a bit short. Stability, progress on many tracks, and access are more the premises that the Technocracy keep their appeal on.<br /> <br /> As a point of comparison, the notion of a gun is certainly a way of ensuring safety, but part of that is because a gun will work for you no matter who you are, what your mindset, destiny, disposition, morality, etc. While the technologies that the Technocracy chases can get arcane and require specialization, the Technocracy's inevitable aim is that the principles that all the technologies work at are technically accessible to the lay person. The Time Table is also a general principle that keeps the Technocracy rolling out new technologies that better address standing problems in it's more unified world, and with that a new norm that sees the masses keeping pace with that roll out. This isn't a strictly &quot;for the people&quot; take, simply that it's easier to have advanced technologies when your baselines are easy to use and grasp. For as totalitarian and imperialistic as the Technocracy is, that rooting of the power in the paradigm into what the unAwakened can personally handle did them a lot of wonders for controlling the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of Trads is that all paradigms would qork everywhere, so I don't know how Stability would be a Crat thing exactly...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T18:40:29-07:00","id":1515813,"title":"","content":"It's definitively propaganda.<br /> <br /> The technocratic world didn't bring safety. True, bygones aren't here eating you. Mostly. And spirits don't possess you. Mostly.<br /> <br /> But on one side, they didn't eliminated the spirit world, nor can they. So spirits, with sufficient efforts, can and will affect your life.<br /> Worse, since the technocracy is convincing the consensus that spirits aren't real, they are therefore also convincing them that various practices done to protect from spirits are bullshit.<br /> <br /> Which means that when spirits do affect you, you can't defend against them, and you don't even realise what is happening to you.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIt also means that people are no longuer able to call on benevolent spirits. Which is something the union's propaganda of course leave behind. The umbra is not just danger, it's also a source of stability. Calling upon the protection of your ancestors, or of the spirit of the house is no longuer possible for humans.<br /> <br /> Hence, humans lost their main protection against circonstances. Since good luck provided by the gods/spirits is no longuer a thing you can call, leaving you in a cold uncaring world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, the union brought massive instability factors in the consensus. Such as mass destruction weapons. The ideas of nuclear weapons, superintelligent IA wanting to exterminate us, or alien invasion are now entrenched into the collective psyche. Making these events more likely to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the techno not only brought danger to the world, but they failed at safeguarding it against the supernatural by taking away our means to defend against it.<br /> <br /> Good jobs guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T18:46:51-07:00","id":1515814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515708#post1515708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safety is a bit short. Stability, progress on many tracks, and access are more the premises that the Technocracy keep their appeal on.<br /> <br /> As a point of comparison, the notion of a gun is certainly a way of ensuring safety, but part of that is because a gun will work for you no matter who you are, what your mindset, destiny, disposition, morality, etc. While the technologies that the Technocracy chases can get arcane and require specialization, the Technocracy's inevitable aim is that the principles that all the technologies work at are technically accessible to the lay person.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the same thing for most non technocrat factions.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bTake the celestial chorus for exemple. Let's imagine they became in control of the consensus, at least as in control of it as the technocracy currently is.<br /> <br /> They convince the world that the one exist, and that all gods are a face of it. And that it wants us to be with him.<br /> <br /> Sure they'll be powerful mages in that world, but it means that everyone will then be able to talkcto the one through their personal vision of god. And hence obtains miracles.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless of the paradigm imposed on the consensus, sleepers will gathers tools from it.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bthe only exception would be a paradigm wjere humans outside of the chosen mages are weak and unworthy of divine/supernatural help. But outside of some nephandi, this is not a common view.<br /> <br /> <br /> This can manifest as rotes/sorcery path becoming available to the common folk. Which is the goal of the council of traditions, at least short term","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:59:35-07:00","id":1515841,"title":"","content":"The Traditions aren't necessarily angling for their Practices to become widely accessable to the Sleepers. I mean, there <i>are </i>the occasional Traditionists who are interested in pursuing that goal; but by and large, the Traditions are about the Awakened: they don't wasn't to spread their beliefs among Sleepers so that the Sleepers can use their Practices; they want to spread their beliefs among the Sleepers so that their own Magick won't be Vulgar. And there's no guarantee that, say, getting the Chorister beliefs firmly ingrained into the Consensus will lead to Sleepers being able to get results by praying; that may be, and by default <i>is, </i>something that's reserved for the priesthood and/or \u201choly men\u201d. Magick is not necessarily a trickle-down affair. <br /> <br /> By contrast: for all their flaws, the Technocracy <i>does</i> strive for their innovations to end up in the hands of the Masses; it is perhaps their single most redeeming quality. That's what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> was talking about in terms of the Union having a Timetable for introducing their innovations to the Masses.<br /> <br /> As well, M20 mentions that \u201cthe Technocratic vision of reality holds the coincidental edge\u2026 because science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics.\u201d (M20 p.613). It's not much of a leap from there to saying that Technocratic innovations are more compatible for use by the Masses than the Traditions' counterparts. That is, in a manner analogous to how the Technocracy has discovered a way to produce Devices with less effort than other mages creating Talismans (i.e., no need for personal Quintessence and Willpower to push the process along), it's entirely possible that their innovations become part of mundane reality more readily than the products of the Traditions do. <br /> <br /> This is speculative, mind you, as nothing in any Mage book anywhere tells you the process by which something transitions from being Coincidental Magick to being non-magical, assuming that's even possible. The closest we get is a box in <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> about how a mage can use something akin to the Wonder creation rules to produce a new sorcerous Path; and while that Path isn't <i>Awakened</i> Magick, it's still magic. Not even the Terranorming rules in the Operative's Dossier lets you redraw the line between Coincidental Magick and Not Magic. For all we know, nothing has <i>ever</i> transitioned from magic to mundane, and everything that's not magical was produced entirely in accordance to the laws of Earthly physics and without any involvement of magic beyond suggesting to the Sleeper inventors what might be possible. And even if it <i>is</i> possible to make the transition, saying that the Traditions are just as capable as the Technocracy of doing so is a <i>preference</i>, not a <i>fact</i>. And there's some reason to think that the Technocracy <i>does</i> have an edge over the Traditions in this regard.<br /> <br /> Note that the last two paragraphs haven't been about the Technocracy, per se; they've been about <i>Enlightened Science</i>, separate from the Technocratic policies. One of my own pet peeves concerning <b>Mage</b> is that it's far too easy to conflate the two. But in the context of M20, it ought to be entirely possible to be an Enlightened Scientist, complete with all of the benefits and drawbacks that come with it, <i>without</i> partaking of the toxic culture of the Technocracy. That said: the Union <i>has</i> been the main proponents of Enlightened Science in the setting as written; and they should get <i>some</i> credit for that, rather than snide remarks about how their supposed contributions to the betterment of humanity don't amount to anything important. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T10:57:45-07:00","id":1515878,"title":"","content":"I think we tend to blur two different distinctions: Awakened/Non-Awakened and Inducted/Non-inducted. Most Traditions mages would very much like it if their practices weren't locked behind the Awakened wall, but far fewer are interested in opening their practices to the uninitiated. <br /> <br /> Even the Technocracy makes this distinction, really. They're not trying to make it so everyone understands the complex laws of the universe (which may or may not have been invented by the Technocracy, who knows), they're trying to make it so anyone can use those inventions that carefully exploit them. Anyone can use a carefully engineered light switch or drive a carefully engineered car, but they have very little interest in a kindergarten education unlocking the secrets of engineering (to use a hyperbolic example). They are quite comfortable with a world where not everyone is inducted but everyone uses the practice.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are the other way around. They would be quite comfortable with a world where everyone is inducted, but they have problems bringing about a world where the uninducted can use their magic. This isn't (usually) for elitist reasons, either. Instead it is because for most Traditions mages the mage is part of the magic. The uninitiated can't use it because initiation is an inseparable part of using magic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T11:41:58-07:00","id":1515881,"title":"","content":"First of all, while the merits and flaws of their approach can be debated, I think it is fair to say that the Technocracy does generally make an effort to protect mundane society from supernatural interference and threats (beyond their own, anyways), and they do make an effort to share the benefits of their power as widely as possible, even if they retain strict control over that power, and are probably spreading its benefits at least in part as a utilitarian move to influence the Consensus in their favour. I think the best interpretation of the Technocracy is of noble intentions corrupted by the struggle they have been fighting and the power they have acquired along the way to fight for those intentions.<br /> <br /> I think looking at how Gauntlet Ratings have changed over around 800 years or so is a bit of a narrow measure of the effects that the Technocracy has had on the lives of Sleepers. Whatever arguments you can make about what the Traditions *could* or *could have* done, the fact is that they did *not* introduce things like public education, civic sanitation, and other mundane aspects of modern life that have drastically increased our lifespans and reduced our vulnerability to the countless cruelties that life can inflict on us. I don't love the Technocracy, but I was won over to this attitude when I read a somewhat-sarcastic argument about how later editions softened their views on Technocrats because the people who gave us mass literacy and toilets probably can't be all bad. That doesn't even enter into things like how Vampires generally treat influencing the top figures of countries like the USA as off-limits in our modern world, because the world the Technocracy has created makes it *too dangerous* for all but the most powerful of Kindred.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy as an institution is absolutely interested in expanding and maintaining its own power and influence, regardless of whatever noble goals or intentions it may otherwise profess, or even authentically pursue. That's one of those punk threads that just runs through almost every World of Darkness interpretation of systems, institutions, and power dynamics.<br /> <br /> Also, just a random thought that I had on the Gauntlet Ratings, but it may be worth considering that changes in the Gauntlet have less to do with the Technocracy and more to do with the larger divide between material and spirit worlds that are a common feature of the various WoD cosmologies. Those splits are generally depicted as starting thousands of years ago, in prehistoric times, so less than a thousand years is maybe not enough time for much of a huge shift there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T17:56:06-07:00","id":1515918,"title":"","content":"If you're not starving to death in the wilds or if you're not agonising in terrible pain in a bed due to smallpox, you can thank the Tecnocracy for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T21:33:07-07:00","id":1515927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515813#post1515813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitively propaganda.<br /> <br /> The technocratic world didn't bring safety. True, bygones aren't here eating you. Mostly. And spirits don't possess you. Mostly.<br /> <br /> But on one side, they didn't eliminated the spirit world, nor can they. So spirits, with sufficient efforts, can and will affect your life.<br /> Worse, since the technocracy is convincing the consensus that spirits aren't real, they are therefore also convincing them that various practices done to protect from spirits are bullshit.<br /> <br /> Which means that when spirits do affect you, you can't defend against them, and you don't even realise what is happening to you.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIt also means that people are no longuer able to call on benevolent spirits. Which is something the union's propaganda of course leave behind. The umbra is not just danger, it's also a source of stability. Calling upon the protection of your ancestors, or of the spirit of the house is no longuer possible for humans.<br /> <br /> Hence, humans lost their main protection against circonstances. Since good luck provided by the gods/spirits is no longuer a thing you can call, leaving you in a cold uncaring world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, the union brought massive instability factors in the consensus. Such as mass destruction weapons. The ideas of nuclear weapons, superintelligent IA wanting to exterminate us, or alien invasion are now entrenched into the collective psyche. Making these events more likely to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the techno not only brought danger to the world, but they failed at safeguarding it against the supernatural by taking away our means to defend against it.<br /> <br /> Good jobs guys</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not an expert on the subject, not at all, but IMO I think that technocracy is more focused on the control of magic, in their opinion making the paradox a bigger impediment for mages is a way to prevent one of them or a faction become too powerful, even because supposedly the maximum potential of a mage is theoretically unlimited if it weren't for the paradox, technocracy is not good, but I also don't believe that traditions would be an example of virtue if o mages had total freedom with their powers, so perhaps this scenario is the least worst in this regard, however something that the technocracy is trying to do would be to monopolize the use of this force known as magic because they believe that it should only be used by a single elite to &quot;avoid&quot; misuse, although that too can, and probably is, a way to gain control. As for supernatural threats and the Umbra, I believe that the technocracy cannot be completely blamed on this point, remember that the beings in the world of WOD don't know about everything there is to know, so IMO the technocracy believed that the paradox applies to everything that later turned out to be a complete mistake and now they try to remedy it, they have a division just to study the Umbra and try to understand it, what they will do with that knowledge is another story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T03:20:50-07:00","id":1515937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515927#post1515927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not an expert on the subject, not at all, but IMO I think that technocracy is more focused on the control of magic, in their opinion making the paradox a bigger impediment for mages is a way to prevent one of them or a faction become too powerful, even because supposedly the maximum potential of a mage is theoretically unlimited if it weren't for the paradox, technocracy is not good, but I also don't believe that traditions would be an example of virtue if o mages had total freedom with their powers, so perhaps this scenario is the least worst in this regard, however something that the technocracy is trying to do would be to monopolize the use of this force known as magic because they believe that it should only be used by a single elite to &quot;avoid&quot; misuse, although that too can, and probably is, a way to gain control. As for supernatural threats and the Umbra, I believe that the technocracy cannot be completely blamed on this point, remember that the beings in the world of WOD don't know about everything there is to know, so IMO the technocracy believed that the paradox applies to everything that later turned out to be a complete mistake and now they try to remedy it, they have a division just to study the Umbra and try to understand it, what they will do with that knowledge is another story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy where the first ones that truly cared. They fed the hungry, they educated the masses and they drove away the darkness.<br /> <br /> The traditions like to talk all the big talk but they never walked the walk. While the starving common men was suffering the cruel realities of the unforgiving harsh world, the &quot;noble&quot; traditionalists where sitting on top of their ivory towers nothing giving 2 cares about those they deemed as lessers. The traditionalists were too busy discussing the sex of the angels to be able to give a helping hand.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Techies filled the bellies of the masses, drove the beasts that hunted man away and tackled the darkness head on. The Technocracy cared. They always cared. It is too cynical to just say that the guys that created vaccines, mass education, mass health, mass production of food, it's cynical to say that those guys just &quot;want power&quot;. That's nonsense. If they just wanted power they would just be another Hermetic house.<br /> <br /> The techies care about the masses. What can be discussed is about their methods. That's another point.<br /> <br /> But I'll be damned if I ever trade the Union for the decadent, solipsistic Traditions. These guys dont really give a damn about the little man, they only care about themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T05:51:32-07:00","id":1515941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515937#post1515937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy where the first ones that truly cared. They fed the hungry, they educated the masses and they drove away the darkness.<br /> <br /> The traditions like to talk all the big talk but they never walked the walk. While the starving common men was suffering the cruel realities of the unforgiving harsh world, the &quot;noble&quot; traditionalists where sitting on top of their ivory towers nothing giving 2 cares about those they deemed as lessers. The traditionalists were too busy discussing the sex of the angels to be able to give a helping hand.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Techies filled the bellies of the masses, drove the beasts that hunted man away and tackled the darkness head on. The Technocracy cared. They always cared. It is too cynical to just say that the guys that created vaccines, mass education, mass health, mass production of food, it's cynical to say that those guys just &quot;want power&quot;. That's nonsense. If they just wanted power they would just be another Hermetic house.<br /> <br /> The techies care about the masses. What can be discussed is about their methods. That's another point.<br /> <br /> But I'll be damned if I ever trade the Union for the decadent, solipsistic Traditions. These guys dont really give a damn about the little man, they only care about themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two things that are important to consider in any discussion of Technocracy vs Traditions and what they did or did not do for humanity.<br /> <br /> The first is what they actually did. The Technocracy did not invent public sanitation or public works. Aqueducts, sewers, mass irrigation systems, etc. all predate the forming of the Order of Reason. Many of them are even attributable to proto-Traditions. Irrigation and calendar systems are deeply intertwined and go back to cultures we would associate with the Verbena. Hospitals are at least partly an invention of the Church (they started out as free lodging, places of hospitality, hence the name. Since they didn't turn away the sick they rapidly became places that priests and doctors would go to tend to the sick). The Order of Hermes has at least as much claim on Roman civic architecture as the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> When the proto-Traditions had the ability to make people\u2019s lives better, many of them clearly did. Moreover, they did so without the knowledge that doing so would change the consensus. That's not something you can say about the Technocracy as they knew from their inception about the consensus.<br /> <br /> The second is what successes are recorded in the history books. Remember that in Mage the history we are familiar with is a sanitized one convenient for the Technocracy. In the same way that they\u2019ve taken credit for ideas that weren\u2019t theirs, they\u2019ve also edited out effectiveness of other philosophies. Whether the Traditions methods were effective or not, the sanitized history will say the same thing: they weren\u2019t.<br /> <br /> None of this is to diminish what the Technocracy has done for humanity in Mage. They\u2019ve had a profound impact; much of it even good. However, when the question is how effective the Technocracy is <i>compared to the Traditions</i>, remember that that is a fundamentally biased question and the answer is not based on what happened in our world but on what happened in the world you explore at your gaming table.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T07:11:50-07:00","id":1515948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515941#post1515941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are two things that are important to consider in any discussion of Technocracy vs Traditions and what they did or did not do for humanity.<br /> <br /> The first is what they actually did. The Technocracy did not invent public sanitation or public works. Aqueducts, sewers, mass irrigation systems, etc. all predate the forming of the Order of Reason. Many of them are even attributable to proto-Traditions. Irrigation and calendar systems are deeply intertwined and go back to cultures we would associate with the Verbena. Hospitals are at least partly an invention of the Church (they started out as free lodging, places of hospitality, hence the name. Since they didn't turn away the sick they rapidly became places that priests and doctors would go to tend to the sick). The Order of Hermes has at least as much claim on Roman civic architecture as the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> When the proto-Traditions had the ability to make people\u2019s lives better, many of them clearly did. Moreover, they did so without the knowledge that doing so would change the consensus. That's not something you can say about the Technocracy as they knew from their inception about the consensus.<br /> <br /> The second is what successes are recorded in the history books. Remember that in Mage the history we are familiar with is a sanitized one convenient for the Technocracy. In the same way that they\u2019ve taken credit for ideas that weren\u2019t theirs, they\u2019ve also edited out effectiveness of other philosophies. Whether the Traditions methods were effective or not, the sanitized history will say the same thing: they weren\u2019t.<br /> <br /> None of this is to diminish what the Technocracy has done for humanity in Mage. They\u2019ve had a profound impact; much of it even good. However, when the question is how effective the Technocracy is <i>compared to the Traditions</i>, remember that that is a fundamentally biased question and the answer is not based on what happened in our world but on what happened in the world you explore at your gaming table.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the point that public sanitation is not something that the Technocracy can lay exclusive claim to inventing. However, I would like to counter that implementation is at least as important as innovation, and the Technocracy seems to be, by and large, the group who has pushed these kinds of technologies on the scale that has created our modern society and the security that comes with it. Aside from physical engineering, the Technocracy also seem to be behind the social engineering that has created much of our modern society.<br /> <br /> &quot;Seem to be&quot; because I think your point about who writes history is also really good. But I must admit that, even from their own point of view, I've never seen the Traditions doing as much collectively to try and improve the lot of Sleepers. Collectively is the important part there; I think individual Traditionalists can be great people who do a lot for the fellow humans. But as institutions, I think the Traditions, at their best, kick the can of helping the Sleepers down the road to &quot;well when we have Mass Ascension, everything is great for everyone,&quot; and at worst simply do not care about anything beyond their own enlightenment, as well as the maintenance and expansion of their power, just like the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I could be absolutely wrong on that, there is a ton of history around individual Traditions, Crafts, etc., that I have never gotten around to reading. I'd be quite open to being corrected on that point, but so far I haven't found any material that pushes back especially hard on that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T07:43:28-07:00","id":1515949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515937#post1515937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy where the first ones that truly cared. They fed the hungry, they educated the masses and they drove away the darkness.<br /> <br /> The traditions like to talk all the big talk but they never walked the walk. While the starving common men was suffering the cruel realities of the unforgiving harsh world, the &quot;noble&quot; traditionalists where sitting on top of their ivory towers nothing giving 2 cares about those they deemed as lessers. The traditionalists were too busy discussing the sex of the angels to be able to give a helping hand.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Techies filled the bellies of the masses, drove the beasts that hunted man away and tackled the darkness head on. The Technocracy cared. They always cared. It is too cynical to just say that the guys that created vaccines, mass education, mass health, mass production of food, it's cynical to say that those guys just &quot;want power&quot;. That's nonsense. If they just wanted power they would just be another Hermetic house.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like they can have power in the same way as tradition mages with their belief, but anyway, I don't know that much about Technocracy in the old days, from what I understand of their concept they are that discussion like there's an a government that will provide you with everything, but you have to give up your creed and your weapons and then it depends on who you trust, in my opinion everything that has to do with a human being has the capacity to go wrong and also we can't rule out that this is also a control tool, I mean they did well as a consequence, but wouldn't nurturing humanity, making it grow and believing in science as a solution be ways to strengthen the paradox? Can't it be just a means to a end? Now it felt like I was advertising for the traditions, but informing only that they are not better on tape.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The techies care about the masses. What can be discussed is about their methods. That's another point. </div> </div> </div>Repeating the questioning, taking care of the masses they take care of the paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'll be damned if I ever trade the Union for the decadent, solipsistic Traditions. These guys dont really give a damn about the little man, they only care about themselves. </div> </div> </div>I believe this can also apply to any supernatural or human in WOD, any of them can choose to do or not do what's best for the whole, some with more difficulty than others, that's true, but everyone prefers to follow their own agenda. I think that's part of the &quot;beauty&quot; of this world. Although I'll be quite honest if I had to team up with someone I think it would have to be the Technocracy really, but that would depend on how things evolve, I think you gave me an idea for a character concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T08:59:10-07:00","id":1515951,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I appreciate the point that public sanitation is not something that the Technocracy can lay exclusive claim to inventing. However, I would like to counter that implementation is at least as important as innovation, and the Technocracy seems to be, by and large, the group who has pushed these kinds of technologies on the scale that has created our modern society and the security that comes with it. Aside from physical engineering, the Technocracy also seem to be behind the social engineering that has created much of our modern society. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Certainly. Keep in mind, though, that when you talk about scale you are using the Technocracy\u2019s preferred yardstick. They favor top down implementations on a wide scale. There\u2019s a lot to be said for the method, both in terms of effectiveness and in terms of control. It\u2019s also something the Traditions can\u2019t match them in. There are precious few moments in the Ascension war where the Traditions could even hope to roll out major infrastructural changes to the world, even if that was an approach they\u2019d take.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Seem to be&quot; because I think your point about who writes history is also really good. But I must admit that, even from their own point of view, I've never seen the Traditions doing as much collectively to try and improve the lot of Sleepers. Collectively is the important part there; I think individual Traditionalists can be great people who do a lot for the fellow humans. But as institutions, I think the Traditions, at their best, kick the can of helping the Sleepers down the road to &quot;well when we have Mass Ascension, everything is great for everyone,&quot; and at worst simply do not care about anything beyond their own enlightenment, as well as the maintenance and expansion of their power, just like the Technocracy. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">One of the fundamental divides between the Traditions and the Technocracy is over individual achievement vs collective effort. The Traditions, by their very nature, will not show as much institutional initiative. They can\u2019t and still be the Freedom side of the Freedom/Security struggle. So if institutional initiative is the benchmark then, again, the Technocracy will just win. It\u2019s their bread and butter. If, however, the question is about the best approach, things become much more complicated.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">After all, the Technocracy may be better at the collective approach, but they are also far more susceptible to institutional corruption. The Traditions may have less problems on that end, but they are more likely to produce a Voormas.</span></span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T18:20:05-07:00","id":1515979,"title":"","content":"And that \u201cindividual achievement\u201d bias among the Traditions partially manifests in their quest for Ascension. This is something that non-Traditionists don't, as a rule, pursue: <i>individual mages </i>do; but neither the Conventions nor (most of) the Crafts do so as institutions. And the main exceptions (the Batini) are <i>former</i> Traditionists. <br /> <br /> As an institution, the Traditions tend to view Sleepers as potential mages; and their idea of bettering the lot of the Sleepers is finding a way to help them Awaken: if you haven't Awakened, how can you ever be the master of your own destiny? But while there's some merit in that, it tends to turn Maslow's hierarchy of needs on its head: <i>first, </i>you should take care of basic needs such as food and shelter, safety and security; <i>then</i> address needs such as relationships and esteem. Self-actualization (i.e., Ascension) comes <i>last</i>. <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maslow%27s_hierarchy_of_needs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img alt=\"Basic (survival, safety), Psychological (relationships, esteem), Self-Fulfillment\" title=\"Maslow&#39;s hierarchy of needs\" width=\"440\" height=\"333\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maslow%27s_hierarchy_of_needs\" data-linktarget=\"1\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Maslow%27s_Hierarchy_of_Needs2.svg/440px-Maslow%27s_Hierarchy_of_Needs2.svg.png\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Maslow%27s_Hierarchy_of_Needs2.svg/440px-Maslow%27s_Hierarchy_of_Needs2.svg.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Maslow%27s_Hierarchy_of_Needs2.svg/440px-Maslow%27s_Hierarchy_of_Needs2.svg.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Maslow&#39;s hierarchy of needs\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a></div><br /> <br /> The Technocracy, for all its flaws, gets the orientation of the Hierarchy of Needs right. The problem is that in their dealing with the Masses, they focus <i>too much</i> on the basic needs and rarely get around to addressing the psychological needs, let alone Awakening and Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T20:56:23-07:00","id":1515982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515918#post1515918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're not starving to death in the wilds or if you're not agonising in terrible pain in a bed due to smallpox, you can thank the Tecnocracy for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry, this is a very, very weak argument.<br /> <br /> First, the Technocracy did not invent all the technology we have, nor are the pioneers in science. Both tech and science were already developing much earlier than the Order of Reason was starting to form. Romans already had irrigation and plumber systems.<br /> <br /> Second, the Technocracy isn't about science. It's about control. They just happen to use the scientific paradigm, just like Etherites, VAs and a lot of other Tradition mages.<br /> <br /> Third, my OP is about a new golden age, considering a complete victory of the Traditions. Which means that modern science/technology/medicine/etc would still exist and be used enough to keep working. Remember, Tradition mages (with the exception of very old masters), do like and use technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515881#post1515881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever arguments you can make about what the Traditions *could* or *could have* done, the fact is that they did *not* introduce things like public education, civic sanitation, and other mundane aspects of modern life that have drastically increased our lifespans and reduced our vulnerability to the countless cruelties that life can inflict on us. I don't love the Technocracy, but I was won over to this attitude when I read a somewhat-sarcastic argument about how later editions softened their views on Technocrats because the people who gave us mass literacy and toilets probably can't be all bad. That doesn't even enter into things like how Vampires generally treat influencing the top figures of countries like the USA as off-limits in our modern world, because the world the Technocracy has created makes it *too dangerous* for all but the most powerful of Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>My answer above applies here. The idea that the Technocracy was responsible for all the good stuff we have now is just wrong. Also, the idea that to have such things, the Technocracy is needed is also wrong. Romans already started developing toilets and that preceeds OoR.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515881#post1515881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, just a random thought that I had on the Gauntlet Ratings, but it may be worth considering that changes in the Gauntlet have less to do with the Technocracy and more to do with the larger divide between material and spirit worlds that are a common feature of the various WoD cosmologies. Those splits are generally depicted as starting thousands of years ago, in prehistoric times, so less than a thousand years is maybe not enough time for much of a huge shift there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The quantity of humans in a region also seem to afect thr Gauntlet rating, so maybe that minor change over time wasn't directly due to Technocracy, but due to population increase. But then, what the hell is the technocracy doing to keep the world safer, if not making the Gauntlet strong? Changing consensus definitely is not enough, since bygones can go around it, and there are lots that *share* the same paradigm that of the Crats (i.e. Weaver spirits)<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Another important point is that the Traditions never had such control over reality and Consensus as the Technocracy have in modern days. Dark Ages was a mess and there wasn't an united Tradition faction.<br /> If we are to discuss Trads vs Crats, we should compare both their views in a victort setting (which for Crats is practically what we had in revised).<br /> Having said that, saying that the Traditions did nothing in a time where they weren't organized nor in control is kinda saying the Crats did nothing when they didn't even exist yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> got quite right. The main struggle between Trads and Crats is Freedom vs. Security and Individualism vs. Colectiveness.<br /> <br /> How much freedom can you have while maintaining security in an acceptable level? Is individual growth and enlightening better than collective?<br /> <br /> Well, the first question is hard to answer. I'd say the main issue here is to get all the Traditions to work along, which might be quite hard (but maybe not impossible, if you consider they got a bit more humble after getting pretty screwed by the Ascension war).<br /> But in a scenario where they do, I believe they could achieve a level of security , the Gauntlet would still exit afterall (and here I add the theory that Technocracy security is mostly propaganda again), while keeping the freedom of all paradigms working at the same time.<br /> <br /> Now, about the second question, I value personal growth over collective/mass &quot;automatic&quot; &quot;enlightement&quot;. The first can lead to true Awakening, while the other is just a mean of providing basic needs and hollow entertainement and facilities for the population with not growth at all (for them as individuals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 06-24-2023, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T21:46:23-07:00","id":1515984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515982#post1515982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the Technocracy isn't about science. It's about control. They just happen to use the scientific paradigm, just like Etherites, VAs and a lot of other Tradition mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's\u2026 overly simplistic. The Technocracy <i>is</i> about control; but it's about a very specific <i>kind </i>of control. The scientific paradigm isn't something that they just happen to use; it's integral to what they are.<br /> <br /> The particular kind of control that the Technocracy represents is right there in their name:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">tech\u00b7noc\u00b7ra\u00b7cy<br /> /tek\u02c8n\u00e4kr\u0259s\u0113/<br /> <br /> <i>noun</i></span><br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">the government or control of society or industry by an elite of technical experts.</span><br /> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</span>Technocrats are an elite of technical experts. And in their hubris, they think they can and should govern or control society or industry. Not because they're control freaks, but because they are experts who have fallen into <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Trap_(British_TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">a trap</a> that's<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200ball too easy for intellectuals to fall into: belief that being smart qualifies you to run other people's lives; that Science holds all the answers. Their dark side is that they represent what happens when you overestimate what science is capable of. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T05:24:23-07:00","id":1516200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515979#post1515979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy, for all its flaws, gets the orientation of the Hierarchy of Needs right. The problem is that in their dealing with the Masses, they focus <i>too much</i> on the basic needs and rarely get around to addressing the psychological needs, let alone Awakening and Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s true, the Technocracy does manage to take care of the more physiological needs of humanity. Sometimes its even their primary intention.<br /> <br /> Even there, though, that\u2019s as much a Technocratic talking point as anything else. Maslow\u2019s hierarchy, like the stages of grief, is one of those things that is more prevalent in entertainment and pop psychology than it is in actual psychological study. The general idea that the human brains tend to prioritize needs in common or universal ways is accepted, as is the idea that it is difficult to focus on other needs when basic biological needs aren\u2019t met. However, the order of those needs, the existence of a strict hierarchy, and the effects of cultural norms on the list are still debated.<br /> <br /> Also we can see plenty of cultural examples throughout history that turn the hierarchy on its head: Aesop\u2019s fables about hunger being better than slavery, Franklin\u2019s comments about giving up freedom for security, cultures that lionize martyrdom or asceticism, etc. So I don\u2019t think we can say that a society where people are well fed but lonely slaves is strictly better, or better ordered, or more moral than one where they are hungry but emotionally and spiritually fulfilled.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I would say that Maslow\u2019s Hierarchy, <i>as we most commonly see it in media</i>, is another Technocratic measuring stick. One they promulgate through the media and one that bolsters and congratulates their focus on security and safety while giving them a pass for their \u201cmore esoteric\u201d failings. When a Traditions mage accuses the Technocracy of turning treating sleepers like lowly animals, \u201cWell fed animals!\u201d isn\u2019t a compelling rebuttal, but \u201cat least we take care of their <i>most important</i> needs!\u201d is.<br /> <br /> But is that true? Are those the most important needs of humanity? That remains one of the core questions of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> And lest we forget the Traditions certainly have their own measuring sticks and talking points in this debate, and I've used a few of them in this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T07:44:44-07:00","id":1516339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515984#post1515984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's\u2026 overly simplistic. The Technocracy <i>is</i> about control; but it's about a very specific <i>kind </i>of control. The scientific paradigm isn't something that they just happen to use; it's integral to what they are.<br /> <br /> The particular kind of control that the Technocracy represents is right there in their name:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">tech\u00b7noc\u00b7ra\u00b7cy<br /> /tek\u02c8n\u00e4kr\u0259s\u0113/<br /> <br /> <i>noun</i></span><br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">the government or control of society or industry by an elite of technical experts.</span><br /> </div><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</span>Technocrats are an elite of technical experts. And in their hubris, they think they can and should govern or control society or industry. Not because they're control freaks, but because they are experts who have fallen into <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Trap_(British_TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">a trap</a> that's<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200ball too easy for intellectuals to fall into: belief that being smart qualifies you to run other people's lives; that Science holds all the answers. Their dark side is that they represent what happens when you overestimate what science is capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the Traditions could have some sort of control, enough to fulfill the basic needs of the masses, including with safety. They just have to work together just enough. And win the war, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T07:50:13-07:00","id":1516340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516339#post1516339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, the Traditions could have some sort of control, enough to fulfill the basic needs of the masses, including with safety. They just have to work together just enough. And win the war, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditions hardly have creeds that are too different for that, which even causes conflicts from what I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T14:13:37-07:00","id":1516363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1515984#post1515984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</span>Technocrats are an elite of technical experts. And in their hubris, they think they can and should govern or control society or industry. Not because they're control freaks, but because they are experts who have fallen into <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Trap_(British_TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">a trap</a> that's<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200ball too easy for intellectuals to fall into: belief that being smart qualifies you to run other people's lives...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not just a Technocratic thing. That's every single Mage. Let's be honest here, Mages are major a-holes. &quot;We are the Enlightened ones&quot;. They believe themselves to be above the cattle... Sorry, I mean the peasants... Sorry, I meant &quot;the masses&quot;, also know as the dumb &quot;sleepers&quot;.<br /> <br /> That goes true for either Technos or Traditions - or others. It's hard not to become a presumptuous a hole when you got the keys of reality at your finger tips, and you're surrounded by endless waves of hordes of primitive barbarians that couldn't possibly fathom the world of enlightenment that you live in.<br /> <br /> The Union is only the hubristic ones and &quot;accidental control freaks&quot; because they are the ones with the power.<br /> <br /> If the crown went into any other group, they would be just as much jerks (if not more so) than the techies; just how the once all powerful Order of Hermes holed themselves in their Ivory Towers and couldnt possibly care less about the ignorant unenlightened peasants around them... &quot;Those are more like animals than humans&quot;... (by the way, for those that do not know, real life hermeticism does indeed see any non-hermetic as mere animals).<br /> <br /> It's not that the Technocrats are bad individuals, but it has more to do with Mages in general being a bunch of arrogant and insufferable a holes, to the extent that even vampires are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T14:19:31-07:00","id":1516365,"title":"","content":"&quot;I know what's best for you... Better than you!&quot;<br /> <br /> That's basically every single Mage EVER. (That's also real world &quot;intellectuals&quot; in a nutshell).<br /> <br /> That's the reason why the techies feel entitled to decide what's best for others. And it's the same reason as any other Mage - I mean, do the Traditions also dont call themselves as either &quot;Enlightened&quot; or &quot;Awaken&quot; as opposed to the hordes (sorry, I meant &quot;masses&quot;) of zombified &quot;sleepers&quot;?<br /> <br /> I love Mage, but let's be honest here, the game should be called &quot;Mage, the arrogant prick&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T14:47:27-07:00","id":1516367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516365#post1516365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I know what's best for you... Better than you!&quot;<br /> <br /> That's basically every single Mage EVER. (That's also real world &quot;intellectuals&quot; in a nutshell).<br /> <br /> That's the reason why the techies feel entitled to decide what's best for others. And it's the same reason as any other Mage - I mean, do the Traditions also dont call themselves as either &quot;Enlightened&quot; or &quot;Awaken&quot; as opposed to the hordes (sorry, I meant &quot;masses&quot;) of zombified &quot;sleepers&quot;?<br /> <br /> I love Mage, but let's be honest here, the game should be called &quot;Mage, the arrogant prick&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think WOD was meant to be like that, a reflection of the worst of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T16:05:32-07:00","id":1516371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516367#post1516367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think WOD was meant to be like that, a reflection of the worst of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but even vampires arent this arrogant. Vampires are selfish monsters, but Mages are self centered arrogant pricks. Two different kinds of bad.<br /> <br /> And it's so bad, that Mages believe themselves to be the heroes of their own stories, when in reality they are all a bunch of tiny little tyrants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T16:13:12-07:00","id":1516372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516340#post1516340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Traditions hardly have creeds that are too different for that, which even causes conflicts from what I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>THey are diferent but they are not mutualy exclusive. They can co-exists. Unlike them and Technocrat creeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T16:20:15-07:00","id":1516374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516365#post1516365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I know what's best for you... Better than you!&quot;<br /> <br /> That's basically every single Mage EVER. (That's also real world &quot;intellectuals&quot; in a nutshell).<br /> <br /> That's the reason why the techies feel entitled to decide what's best for others. And it's the same reason as any other Mage - I mean, do the Traditions also dont call themselves as either &quot;Enlightened&quot; or &quot;Awaken&quot; as opposed to the hordes (sorry, I meant &quot;masses&quot;) of zombified &quot;sleepers&quot;?<br /> <br /> I love Mage, but let's be honest here, the game should be called &quot;Mage, the arrogant prick&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I get what you're saying, I think you're missing my point. It isn't about who's better, Traditions or Technocrats; it's about <i>how they're different from each other. </i><br /> <br /> Yes, hubris is a common feature of all mages; even the Choristers, who make a strong push toward practicing humility, somehow manage to find a way to twist that into a kind of hubris. But \u201cI know what's best for you, better than you do\u201d, while not unique to the Technocracy, is in effect the Technocracy's signature hubris: scientism. The Traditions and the Disparates are a very diverse lot; and while some of them (such as the Order of Hermes) have a sort of intellectual hubris, others are far from being intellectuals: the aforementioned Choristers consider faith in the One to be more important than rationalism; the Cult of Ecstasy and Verbena favor a more intuitional mindset; Euthanatoi value mystical insight and moral judgment when administering the Good Death, not cold rationality; Dreamspeakers value the ability to straddle barriers and commune with the Other over rationality; and so on. <br /> <br /> They're still arrogant so-and-sos who consider themselves to be better than Sleepers; I'm not arguing that point. But among the Traditions, this arrogance tends to manifest more as not particularly caring about the standard of living of the average Sleeper; some even argue that the more of a plight the Sleepers go through, the more motivation the Sleepers have to improve their lot, which leads to more of them Awakening \u2014 which is what the Traditions <i>really</i> care about where Sleepers are concerned: leading people into Awakenings. \u201cI know what's best for you better than you do\u201d manifests, if at all, in trying to force people to Awaken who don't want to. After all, why would anyone not want to Awaken?<br /> <br /> By contrast, Technocrats generally don't care about leading people to Enlightenment: if it happens, snatch them up and integrate them into the elite; of it doesn't happen, no big deal. In fact, you'll find arguments among them that every Awakening is potentially a new Marauder or Nephandus, and that a Mass Awakening would be a disaster as large numbers of madmen and monsters would get access to power that can destroy the world. But they <i>do</i> care about improving the everyday lives of the Masses; and through such measures as the Timetable, they seek to do so in the safest way possible. <br /> <br /> And more importantly, they <i>are</i> intellectuals; and to them, Science and Technology are the ultimate expressions of the triumph of the intellectual over the idiot. Heck, they even think that their Enlightened Science makes them better than the Superstitionists, as they call other Awakened \u2014 as evinced by the very term \u201cSuperstitionist\u201d. <b>They think that every problem in the world can be solved by smart people thinking things through and coming up with the most rational solution.</b> And that belief is the heart of Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> By and large, the Traditions don't agree. They have their <i>own</i> forms of hubris; but their big innovation is the idea that there isn't just one right answer, and that there are many paths that contribute something of value: due to the ecumenism that they cultivate in their members, even an intellectual in the ranks of the Traditions will tell you that intellectuals (\u201csmart people thinking rationally\u201d) is just one way of doing things; and that there's a time and place for faith, or crazy wisdom, or several other mindsets which can produce results through an Awakened Focus. \u201cBeing smart and thinking rationally\u201d has its limits, and also isn't for everyone. <br /> <hr /><br /> And that's my main point: the Union isn't about control, per se; it's about intellectualism, the idea that educated people (\u201can elite of experts\u201d) should be in charge. Technocracy. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T16:56:01-07:00","id":1516378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516371#post1516371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but even vampires arent this arrogant. Vampires are selfish monsters, but Mages are self centered arrogant pricks. Two different kinds of bad.<br /> <br /> And it's so bad, that Mages believe themselves to be the heroes of their own stories, when in reality they are all a bunch of tiny little tyrants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because in the case of vampires they don't want to change anything, they just act on their own and do what they need to with it, in the end they are monsters and assume that, whereas mages, they believe in something and follow that path , but it's not something 100% logical, more a creed and well, this is something that happens with certain regularity in those who believe in some cause, and it's quite annoying, I won't deny it, but in their case it seems that their avatar compel it.<br /> <br /> Writing this comment I came across some strange thoughts.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:19:29-07:00","id":1516382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516372#post1516372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THey are diferent but they are not mutualy exclusive. They can co-exists. Unlike them and Technocrat creeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coexisting is one thing, but uniting is another, just look at the stereotypes that each creed has about the others, I doubt that many believe that the VA and SoE still not a part of the technocracy, or that the Euthanatos are not simply a cult of killers, CoE I won't even mention because this triggers me, CC are... the Chorus, I don't know how to explain without talking nonsense, Akashic I think, I just think, that they are too static to do anything effectively. Even ignoring all that, assuming it wasn't technocracy to give traditions a common enemy I think they would be looking for a way to be the new technocracy so to speak... that's something to think about indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:26:40-07:00","id":1516383,"title":"","content":"I'd say less that their Avatars compel it and more that their Avatars are shaped by it. Or rather, it's a two-way street; determining what comes from the Avatar and what comes from the mage, or even whether that distinction is even meaningful, is a difficult question; intentionally so.<br /> <br /> That said, in my own head-canon, Geniuses tend to be Circumspect by default (with the Demented Eidolon Flaw representing any non-Circumspect Genius) whereas other Avatars tend not to be Circumspect. This may have something to do with Conditioning; but I apply that rule to <i>all</i> Enlightened Scientists, not just those in the Earthside Conventions: the Void Engineers, Navalon, and independent Enlightened Scientists <i>also</i> have Circumspect Avatars by default, despite being free from Conditioning. So the idea that there's some sort of connection between your Avatar/Genius and your Focus isn't new to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-27-2023, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:30:26-07:00","id":1516385,"title":"","content":"I imagine that an avatar can be affected by the person, but it compels them to want to ascend, but as they don't know how to do it, they follow a creed in this attempt in order to satisfy this &quot;hunger&quot; that the avatar generates. I'm not sure I explained it correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:33:21-07:00","id":1516387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516382#post1516382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coexisting is one thing, but uniting is another, just look at the stereotypes that each creed has about the others, I doubt that many believe that the VA and SoE still not a part of the technocracy, or that the Euthanatos are not simply a cult of killers, CoE I won't even mention because this triggers me, CC are... the Chorus, I don't know how to explain without talking nonsense, Akashic I think, I just think, that they are too static to do anything effectively. Even ignoring all that, assuming it wasn't technocracy to give traditions a common enemy I think they would be looking for a way to be the new technocracy so to speak... that's something to think about indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, \u201cunited only by a common enemy\u201d is a Disparate Alliance thing, not a Traditions thing; and it's part of the reason why the Alliance is so weak and fragile. I see the Traditions as being invested in the idea that \u201cwe're all doing the same thing, just in different ways\u201d \u2014 an idea that's rare outside of the Traditions and flatly rejected by the Technocracy. While there's infighting in the Traditions, it's tempered by their shared pseudo-ecumenical worldview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:39:41-07:00","id":1516388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516385#post1516385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that an avatar can be affected by the person, but it compels them to want to ascend, but as they don't know how to do it, they follow a creed in this attempt in order to satisfy this &quot;hunger&quot; that the avatar generates. I'm not sure I explained it correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>In sure that's a popular belief among the Traditions. But I also tend to view the pursuit of Ascension as something that's more prominent among the Traditions than outside of them. It's not that, say, the Bata'a or the Templars don't have their Avatars nudging then towards Seekings and higher Arete; but they tend not to pursue Ascension with the same ferver that the Traditions do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T18:11:00-07:00","id":1516393,"title":"","content":"Look, I don't see how traditions could have so much mutual respect, I mean, they sometimes act like something another tradition repudiates. And an alliance made in this context can be fragile, but you know how it is in times of desperation/necessity, sometimes you only have bad choices and you try to do the lesser of evils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T18:24:09-07:00","id":1516398,"title":"","content":"Like I said, there <i>is </i>infighting between them. But they've <i>been </i>allies for <i>centuries; </i>that doesn't happen without them developing <i>some </i>degree of mutual respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T19:00:52-07:00","id":1516400,"title":"","content":"I don't know what to tell you anymore, for me you can be a person's ally and still not like them, and not respect them, you just have to help each other or do your part (which in terms of context is questionable) I myself have worked with people for a considerable time and she only does her part, they put it on the table and if there's a problem it's not her fault, and that's if she does something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T19:07:21-07:00","id":1516402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516387#post1516387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, \u201cunited only by a common enemy\u201d is a Disparate Alliance thing, not a Traditions thing; and it's part of the reason why the Alliance is so weak and fragile. I see the Traditions as being invested in the idea that \u201cwe're all doing the same thing, just in different ways\u201d \u2014 an idea that's rare outside of the Traditions and flatly rejected by the Technocracy. While there's infighting in the Traditions, it's tempered by their shared pseudo-ecumenical worldview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently realised that WoD, but Mage most of all, is almost exclusively a gnostic/hermetic/theosophical guide in a light hearted game form. The hermetic (the real life kind, not the game one) idea that every single religion and every single philosophy in the world is part of the same diamond of &quot;gnosis&quot; (divine revelation), facets of the same &quot;divine truth&quot;, is absolutely real life hermeticism.<br /> <br /> Heck, the very groups in Mage are totally theosophical. What does the Celestial Chorus represents after all? Nothing. They represent nothing. They were supposed to be &quot;Christian Mages&quot;, but instead they are just the &quot;Western Society of Theosophy&quot;. As are the Ahl-I-Batin. As are the Akashics.<br /> <br /> The very idea about the &quot;Avatars&quot; and about &quot;The One&quot; and &quot;Ascension&quot;, that's 101% Gnosticism. &quot;Awakening&quot; is just &quot;gnosis&quot;, the idea that you open your eyes to the truth due to divine revelation - aka GOD speaks inside your mind the truth.<br /> <br /> And what is the &quot;gnostic truth&quot;? That WE ARE GOD.<br /> <br /> That's right, we are pieces of the divine (&quot;The One&quot;) that got fragmented, and now our job is to &quot;remember that we are God&quot; (aka to &quot;ascend&quot;).<br /> <br /> Sounds familiar to anyone?<br /> <br /> I begin to suspect that the writers of Mage are a bunch of gnostic/hermetic cultists.<br /> <br /> Also, take Vampire and Demon the Fallen and you'll find the ideas about the evil &quot;Demiurge&quot; there<br /> <br /> * Gnostic belief is that the material world is an illusory prison built by the Demiurge - the false God (or simply the Devil) to imprison our souls and prevent us to remember that we are God and prevent us to reunite with &quot;The One&quot;. Sounds familiar? That's Gnosticism... And this lunatic cult sounds eerily similar to WoD games.<br /> Heck, Werewolves literally have &quot;Gnosis&quot; on their sheets...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T19:09:24-07:00","id":1516403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516400#post1516400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what to tell you anymore, for me you can be a person's ally and still not like them, and not respect them, you just have to help each other or do your part (which in terms of context is questionable) I myself have worked with people for a considerable time and she only does her part, they put it on the table and if there's a problem it's not her fault, and that's if she does something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I repeat: centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-27-2023, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T19:51:40-07:00","id":1516407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516402#post1516402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recently realised that WoD, but Mage most of all, is almost exclusively a gnostic/hermetic/theosophical guide in a light hearted game form. The hermetic (the real life kind, not the game one) idea that every single religion and every single philosophy in the world is part of the same diamond of &quot;gnosis&quot; (divine revelation), facets of the same &quot;divine truth&quot;, is absolutely real life hermeticism.<br /> <br /> Heck, the very groups in Mage are totally theosophical. What does the Celestial Chorus represents after all? Nothing. They represent nothing. They were supposed to be &quot;Christian Mages&quot;, but instead they are just the &quot;Western Society of Theosophy&quot;. As are the Ahl-I-Batin. As are the Akashics.<br /> <br /> The very idea about the &quot;Avatars&quot; and about &quot;The One&quot; and &quot;Ascension&quot;, that's 101% Gnosticism. &quot;Awakening&quot; is just &quot;gnosis&quot;, the idea that you open your eyes to the truth due to divine revelation - aka GOD speaks inside your mind the truth.<br /> <br /> And what is the &quot;gnostic truth&quot;? That WE ARE GOD.<br /> <br /> That's right, we are pieces of the divine (&quot;The One&quot;) that got fragmented, and now our job is to &quot;remember that we are God&quot; (aka to &quot;ascend&quot;).<br /> <br /> Sounds familiar to anyone?<br /> <br /> I begin to suspect that the writers of Mage are a bunch of gnostic/hermetic cultists.<br /> <br /> Also, take Vampire and Demon the Fallen and you'll find the ideas about the evil &quot;Demiurge&quot; there<br /> <br /> * Gnostic belief is that the material world is an illusory prison built by the Demiurge - the false God (or simply the Devil) to imprison our souls and prevent us to remember that we are God and prevent us to reunite with &quot;The One&quot;. Sounds familiar? That's Gnosticism... And this lunatic cult sounds eerily similar to WoD games.<br /> Heck, Werewolves literally have &quot;Gnosis&quot; on their sheets...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been aware of those overtones for a while now (though I haven't seen them spelled out so blatantly before) \u2014 which is part of why I try to restrict those elements to being Tradition beliefs instead of being fundamental truths. Just because the Hermetics, Choristers, Akashayana, and so on are pseudo-Theosophist, that doesn't mean that groups like the Wu Lung, Ngoma, Bata'a, Hypollytoi, or Templars have to be. And the Technocracy <i>shouldn't</i> be.<br /> <br /> So by changing the elements inspired by Gnosticism, Hermeticism, and Theosophy to being part of an in-setting faction's Focus instead of being an absolute truth of the setting, the groups outside of the Traditions are more free to <i>not</i> be beholden to those elements. It doesn't mean that they <i>can't</i> be; the Batini, as you say, are. But they don't <i>have to</i> be.<br /> <br /> Play this pseudo-Gnosticism shared among the Traditions as part of the reason why they're still together after centuries. And this further helps differentiate the Traditions from the Disparates, to whom they'd otherwise look almost identical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-28-2023, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:04:35-07:00","id":1516445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516402#post1516402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heck, the very groups in Mage are totally theosophical. What does the Celestial Chorus represents after all? Nothing. They represent nothing. They were supposed to be &quot;Christian Mages&quot;, but instead they are just the &quot;Western Society of Theosophy&quot;. As are the Ahl-I-Batin. As are the Akashics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. Though I view that as a holdover from an earlier time when Mage was written as 19th and 20th century occult philosophy vs modernity. I\u2019ve spent quite some time trying to rework the Traditions so that they better map to what they claim to represent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The very idea about the &quot;Avatars&quot; and about &quot;The One&quot; and &quot;Ascension&quot;, that's 101% Gnosticism. &quot;Awakening&quot; is just &quot;gnosis&quot;, the idea that you open your eyes to the truth due to divine revelation - aka GOD speaks inside your mind the truth. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026<br /> <br /> That's right, we are pieces of the divine (&quot;The One&quot;) that got fragmented, and now our job is to &quot;remember that we are God&quot; (aka to &quot;ascend&quot;).<br /> <br /> Sounds familiar to anyone? </div> </div> </div>The Matrix. The Truman Show. They Live. Dark City. The Lego Movie even has Will Ferrell playing the demiurge.<br /> <br /> Gnosticism is a very easy idea to make a story around. It has a natural tension between what seems to be and what actually is. It\u2019s endlessly adaptable. It doesn\u2019t lock you in to a specific religious or moral system. It naturally maps well to specific steps on the hero\u2019s journey. Etc.<br /> <br /> Also, because we have only a general understanding of gnostic theology, we tend to overapply the label (hence \u201cendlessly adaptable\u201d for movie purposes). However, many, many secret and/or occult societies promote the idea that there is a greater truth open to the enlightened (i.e. themselves). That\u2019s even the idea behind Plato\u2019s cave allegory. So it\u2019s a trend that goes back well before Gnosticism.<br /> \u200b<br /> Mage has an unfortunate tendency to blur the lines between the beliefs of some factions and the rules of the game. One of the ways this manifests is in expounding upon things like the shards of the One as if they are known truths of the game. The Technocracy gets its share of these too, if you know where to look. It's not a sign that the game is promoting a specific philosophy, but that it is built on a mishmash of various convenient philosophies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T07:12:02-07:00","id":1516453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516445#post1516445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Mage has an unfortunate tendency to blur the lines between the beliefs of some factions and the rules of the game. One of the ways this manifests is in expounding upon things like the shards of the One as if they are known truths of the game. The Technocracy gets its share of these too, if you know where to look. It's not a sign that the game is promoting a specific philosophy, but that it is built on a mishmash of various convenient philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The emphasis on the whole &quot;Avatar&quot; thing is also an unfortunate subset of that. Just by having Avatars, the Hermetics (and the Theosophic Choristers) are already proven right by default.<br /> <br /> I think it would be better that the Hermetics believed in the whole &quot;Avatar thing&quot;, while others believe it comes from the &quot;soul&quot; or even the mind or &quot;quantum-babble&quot; or scientific principles, and to do away with all the Avatar related mechanics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T07:37:01-07:00","id":1516456,"title":"","content":"My own take on it is that an Avatar is \u201cwhatever it is that lets you do Magick\u201d. Which is extremely vague; but that's intentional. <br /> <br /> But rather than doing away with Avatar related mechanics, I prefer to lean into the ability to customize them, to represent what the Avatar is <i>in your case. </i>If you come from a belief system where that thing that lets you do Magick doesn't talk to you, take Circumspect Avatar; if your Avatar is a thing that you can carry around with you, add Phylactery; and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T07:53:00-07:00","id":1516457,"title":"","content":"I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> on this. While Avatars initially seem like one coherent idea, they are actually all over the place in behavior, form, function, etc. Indeed Avatars seem to inhabit a place of multiple, contradictory presentations. While some writeups treat them as external to the soul, others tie them deeply to reincarnation (another thing that is treated inconsistently). Even the sphere mechanics can't seem to quantify them in any specific way. <br /> <br /> We are very specifically not locked into any one way of thinking about Avatars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:47:30-07:00","id":1516485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516400#post1516400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what to tell you anymore, for me you can be a person's ally and still not like them, and not respect them, you just have to help each other or do your part (which in terms of context is questionable) I myself have worked with people for a considerable time and she only does her part, they put it on the table and if there's a problem it's not her fault, and that's if she does something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Traditions do not need to like each other. They have to respect on do their part, just like your co-worker. Of course big groups will have infight. But if the Trads wins the war and do the minimum (which they aready do) of respecting each other and following the rules, they would make it work. By your logic, the Traditions wouldn't even exist in any scenario.<br /> <br /> About the differences in paradigms, this is covered in Guide to the Traditions in how strict the paradigms are. The Traditions tend to have an Open paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:51:40-07:00","id":1516487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516402#post1516402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recently realised that WoD, but Mage most of all, is almost exclusively a gnostic/hermetic/theosophical guide in a light hearted game form. The hermetic (the real life kind, not the game one) idea that every single religion and every single philosophy in the world is part of the same diamond of &quot;gnosis&quot; (divine revelation), facets of the same &quot;divine truth&quot;, is absolutely real life hermeticism.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are describing *one* paradigm in-game. There are several others and some do not include believing in a &quot;The One&quot; or in a False God.<br /> <br /> Same for avatars. Technos believe in Genius. Each Tradition, to be honest, each mage will have their own take on Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:56:37-07:00","id":1516489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516457#post1516457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> on this. While Avatars initially seem like one coherent idea, they are actually all over the place in behavior, form, function, etc. Indeed Avatars seem to inhabit a place of multiple, contradictory presentations. While some writeups treat them as external to the soul, others tie them deeply to reincarnation (another thing that is treated inconsistently). Even the sphere mechanics can't seem to quantify them in any specific way.<br /> <br /> We are very specifically not locked into any one way of thinking about Avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, except that the books dont treat them this way. The Avatar sure is a thing for the game, there's no dispute there. You may say that all Techies have a Circumspected Avatar, but that's headcanon and it still relays to the Avatar!<br /> <br /> Instead, the Disadvantage &quot;Philactery&quot; could have &quot;your magic comes from an object. You cant do magic without it&quot;. But instead, it says that YOUR AVATAR is imprisoned in an object.<br /> <br /> Hermetics and Choristers and whatever could have an advantage that is something of the likes of &quot;You hear your own Soul's voice&quot;, or maybe call it &quot;Gnosis&quot; (aha!) claiming that &quot;you are guided by Divine Revelation (Gnosis). There's a &quot;voice&quot; that propels you to do stuff&quot;. That would mean that Hermetics and Choristers are lunatics that hear voices (which they call as &quot;Avatars&quot;), but a Chakravanti do NOT.<br /> <br /> This would represent belief. Instead, the game world makes it clear that Avatars are absolutely real, even if you dont know all of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:03:16-07:00","id":1516492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516487#post1516487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are describing *one* paradigm in-game. There are several others and some do not include believing in a &quot;The One&quot; or in a False God.<br /> <br /> Same for avatars. Technos believe in Genius. Each Tradition, to be honest, each mage will have their own take on Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesnt matter what they believe. They are wrong, it's as simple as that.<br /> <br /> Avatars are the real deal in MtA, and Technocrats are self deluded idiots. That's my beef with it. The game is ABSOLUTELY Gnostic in its cosmology. The whole thing about &quot;Geniuses&quot; is just more techno-babble to justify the existance of the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> This wouldnt matter however if the &quot;Avatar&quot; was just an advantage (or disadvantage maybe?) for Hermetics and Choristers who believe that the voices in their heads come from &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; and no other group had such a trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:28:05-07:00","id":1516498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516492#post1516492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesnt matter what they believe. They are wrong, it's as simple as that.<br /> <br /> Avatars are the real deal in MtA, and Technocrats are self deluded idiots. That's my beef with it. The game is ABSOLUTELY Gnostic in its cosmology. The whole thing about &quot;Geniuses&quot; is just more techno-babble to justify the existance of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> This wouldnt matter however if the &quot;Avatar&quot; was just an advantage (or disadvantage maybe?) for Hermetics and Choristers who believe that the voices in their heads come from &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; and no other group had such a trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your arguments are exaclty some Hermetic would say in-game. Out of game, however, they do not specify exaclty what an Avatar is (intentionally). Out of game true paradigm is just that magick works because people believe it. That's it. There no demiurge or The One defined.<br /> <br /> Hermetics (or gnostisism) is just as right or wrong as any other paradigm, including Techs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:44:04-07:00","id":1516503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516489#post1516489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, except that the books dont treat them this way. The Avatar sure is a thing for the game, there's no dispute there. You may say that all Techies have a Circumspected Avatar, but that's headcanon and it still relays to the Avatar!<br /> <br /> Instead, the Disadvantage &quot;Philactery&quot; could have &quot;your magic comes from an object. You cant do magic without it&quot;. But instead, it says that YOUR AVATAR is imprisoned in an object.<br /> <br /> Hermetics and Choristers and whatever could have an advantage that is something of the likes of &quot;You hear your own Soul's voice&quot;, or maybe call it &quot;Gnosis&quot; (aha!) claiming that &quot;you are guided by Divine Revelation (Gnosis). There's a &quot;voice&quot; that propels you to do stuff&quot;. That would mean that Hermetics and Choristers are lunatics that hear voices (which they call as &quot;Avatars&quot;), but a Chakravanti do NOT.<br /> <br /> This would represent belief. Instead, the game world makes it clear that Avatars are absolutely real, even if you dont know all of them</div> </div> </div> </div>There is something that the rules call an Avatar, and it has specific mechanical effects, but it isn't clear what this actually is in universe. It isn't clear if it is something everyone has or it is limited to a lucky few (though Mage has been drifting more and more towards the former. It isn't clear if it is a separate entity or just the nature of the human soul. It isn't even clear if it is the same thing each time.<br /> <br /> As I recall, some Techies actually theorize that the way the Avatar manifests for most Tradis is some kind of alien entity hijacking something that's supposed to be an innate human ability. You might think that's just rationalization, but it is quite possible they are right.<br /> <br /> In my experience, being vague about what the Avatar really is only benefits the game. Getting into specifics usually locks down elements of the game that don't need locking.<br /> <br /> And note, the Avatar doesn't have to be belief based to be variable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-28-2023, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:02:09-07:00","id":1516507,"title":"","content":"Some of it might be a legacy from Ars Magica. I never played it, but I heard it had a much stronger hermetic focus. Also, for the sake of clarity, the authors had to stick with one model to transport the rules. Avatar in this case becomes a keyword that describes a concept a player is familiar with. The more open you get with language, the less precise it becomes. Shaka, when the walls fell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:16:12-07:00","id":1516508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516498#post1516498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your arguments are exaclty some Hermetic would say in-game. Out of game, however, they do not specify exaclty what an Avatar is (intentionally). Out of game true paradigm is just that magick works because people believe it. That's it. There no demiurge or The One defined.<br /> <br /> Hermetics (or gnostisism) is just as right or wrong as any other paradigm, including Techs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the books describe &quot;Avatar this, Avatar that&quot; when explaining both the mechanics and the cosmology of the world, and this is not done in character (as in, a hermetic explaining his theories).<br /> <br /> The Avatar is not set on stone as something defined, but IT IS SOMETHING.<br /> <br /> You dont get atheist materialist technocrats because you cant just have someone join the &quot;school for the exceptionally gifted&quot; to learn all the precepts of space/time warp engineering, because that only happens for the &quot;enlightened&quot; that learned those hardcore scientific concepts after surviving a car accident or being &quot;abducted by aliens&quot;. And those people can even be idiots who know nothing about &quot;hypereconomics&quot; but somehow they become &quot;Enlightened&quot; out of the blue, and have a &quot;Genius&quot;, even if their Int attribute is 1 amd they dont have a single dot on any STEM skills","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:03:44-07:00","id":1516530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516453#post1516453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be better that the Hermetics believed in the whole &quot;Avatar thing&quot;, while others believe it comes from the &quot;soul&quot; or even the mind or &quot;quantum-babble&quot; or scientific principles, and to do away with all the Avatar related mechanics</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516489#post1516489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, except that the books dont treat them this way. The Avatar sure is a thing for the game, there's no dispute there. You may say that all Techies have a Circumspected Avatar, but that's headcanon and it still relays to the Avatar!<br /> <br /> Instead, the Disadvantage &quot;Philactery&quot; could have &quot;your magic comes from an object. You cant do magic without it&quot;. But instead, it says that YOUR AVATAR is imprisoned in an object.<br /> <br /> Hermetics and Choristers and whatever could have an advantage that is something of the likes of &quot;You hear your own Soul's voice&quot;, or maybe call it &quot;Gnosis&quot; (aha!) claiming that &quot;you are guided by Divine Revelation (Gnosis). There's a &quot;voice&quot; that propels you to do stuff&quot;. That would mean that Hermetics and Choristers are lunatics that hear voices (which they call as &quot;Avatars&quot;), but a Chakravanti do NOT.<br /> <br /> This would represent belief. Instead, the game world makes it clear that Avatars are absolutely real, even if you dont know all of them</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be arguing contrary points. On the one hand, you're suggesting that we should ignore the rules for the Avatar; on the other hand, you seem to be staying that if we <i>don't</i> ignore those rules as you suggest, then we need to take everything the books say extremely literally; the option of interpreting the rules creatively seems to be off the table for you.<br /> <br /> Yes, \u201cmost Technocrats have Circumspect Avatars\u201d is head-canon. I said as much when I suggested the idea. You know what else is head-canon? \u201cIgnore all mechanics for Avatars.\u201d As well, the mechanics for Circumspect Avatar can be used to describe a mage whose source of Magick doesn't talk to them.<br /> <br /> Yes, the text for Phylactery talks about the Avatar being housed within an object. But the important thing about that Flaw is that it represents the mage's source of power coming from an object. The fact that it's described in terms of an Avatar is less important; and you can keep the Phylactery Flaw's mechanics without keeping Avatars by reinterpreting the Flaw in a way that refers to \u201csource of Magick\u201d instead of \u201cAvatar\u201d.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516508#post1516508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the books describe &quot;Avatar this, Avatar that&quot; when explaining both the mechanics and the cosmology of the world, and this is not done in character (as in, a hermetic explaining his theories).<br /> <br /> The Avatar is not set on stone as something defined, but IT IS SOMETHING.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already said as much: it is the mage's source of Magick. That's \u201cSomething\u201d. The other details of what an Avatar is can be changed by appropriate Merits or Flaws, or by Storyteller fiat \u2014 much like removing them entirely, as you suggested doing, is done by Storyteller fiat. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516508#post1516508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You dont get atheist materialist technocrats because you cant just have someone join the &quot;school for the exceptionally gifted&quot; to learn all the precepts of space/time warp engineering, because that only happens for the &quot;enlightened&quot; that learned those hardcore scientific concepts after surviving a car accident or being &quot;abducted by aliens&quot;. And those people can even be idiots who know nothing about &quot;hypereconomics&quot; but somehow they become &quot;Enlightened&quot; out of the blue, and have a &quot;Genius&quot;, even if their Int attribute is 1 amd they dont have a single dot on any STEM skills</div> </div> </div> </div>The Enlightened Scientist does indeed need some moment in his life where he made a breakthrough that allowed him to realize that he can do more with Enlightened Science than he previously thought. But that doesn't mean that that moment of inspiration can't be linked to being smart and educated.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it makes a fair amount of sense for the nature of the Avatar/Genius to reflect (or be reflected by) the way the Awakening/Enlightenment played out, so that people who are atheist materialists are more likely to Enlighten with Geniuses that are Circumspect and can be thought of by the Scientist as \u201cI'm just that clever\u201d; meanwhile, a devout Christian who Awakens is more likely to find herself with a \u201cguardian angel\u201d that guides her. If this is the case, you probably <i>won't</i> find many Technocrats who are idiots with no education. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:48:34-07:00","id":1516561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516485#post1516485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Traditions do not need to like each other. They have to respect on do their part, just like your co-worker. Of course big groups will have infight. But if the Trads wins the war and do the minimum (which they aready do) of respecting each other and following the rules, they would make it work. By your logic, the Traditions wouldn't even exist in any scenario.<br /> <br /> About the differences in paradigms, this is covered in Guide to the Traditions in how strict the paradigms are. The Traditions tend to have an Open paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only think that you are oversimplifying something that should be more complicated, the traditions look down on each other because they see their creeds as... eccentric, to say the least, I don't think all of them are capable of being so open-minded to the point where they respect each other, they only team up out of necessity and they kind of know what can happen if they don't, people do that and they find ways to make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:01:57-07:00","id":1516565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516530#post1516530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to be arguing contrary points. On the one hand, you're suggesting that we should ignore the rules for the Avatar; on the other hand, you seem to be staying that if we <i>don't</i> ignore those rules as you suggest, then we need to take everything the books say extremely literally; the option of interpreting the rules creatively seems to be off the table for you.<br /> <br /> Yes, \u201cmost Technocrats have Circumspect Avatars\u201d is head-canon. I said as much when I suggested the idea. You know what else is head-canon? \u201cIgnore all mechanics for Avatars.\u201d As well, the mechanics for Circumspect Avatar can be used to describe a mage whose source of Magick doesn't talk to them.<br /> <br /> Yes, the text for Phylactery talks about the Avatar being housed within an object. But the important thing about that Flaw is that it represents the mage's source of power coming from an object. The fact that it's described in terms of an Avatar is less important; and you can keep the Phylactery Flaw's mechanics without keeping Avatars by reinterpreting the Flaw in a way that refers to \u201csource of Magick\u201d instead of \u201cAvatar\u201d.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've already said as much: it is the mage's source of Magick. That's \u201cSomething\u201d. The other details of what an Avatar is can be changed by appropriate Merits or Flaws, or by Storyteller fiat \u2014 much like removing them entirely, as you suggested doing, is done by Storyteller fiat.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Enlightened Scientist does indeed need some moment in his life where he made a breakthrough that allowed him to realize that he can do more with Enlightened Science than he previously thought. But that doesn't mean that that moment of inspiration can't be linked to being smart and educated.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it makes a fair amount of sense for the nature of the Avatar/Genius to reflect (or be reflected by) the way the Awakening/Enlightenment played out, so that people who are atheist materialists are more likely to Enlighten with Geniuses that are Circumspect and can be thought of by the Scientist as \u201cI'm just that clever\u201d; meanwhile, a devout Christian who Awakens is more likely to find herself with a \u201cguardian angel\u201d that guides her. If this is the case, you probably <i>won't</i> find many Technocrats who are idiots with no education.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you are interpreting things into YOUR headcanon. But that's NOT how the books interpret things. In tne books, Avatars are REAL. Whatever their exact nature is.<br /> <br /> And no, they are NOT just a &quot;source of magic(k)&quot;. They talk inside your head.<br /> <br /> And for them not to talk, you need a special trait.<br /> <br /> And no, not all Techies get Circumspect Avatar. Many techies also get their &quot;Geniuses&quot; schizophrenic voice inside their heads.<br /> <br /> Also, those voices arent just schizophrenia, just phantom voices; they actually have VALUABLE information, sometimes the kind of which the Mage himself couldnt possibly have. So no, the game itself contradicts everything you're saying. Avatars are VERY real, and are the real thing. Sure, you can <b>personally interpret</b> them away, but that's not what the books say.<br /> <br /> Also, Im not suggesting any headcanon, Im simply stating a fact that Mage has a heavily gnostic philosophy behind it, and if the purpose was to truly make it so that &quot;anything goes&quot;, than Hermeticism shouldnt be <b>The Truth</b> (because it is), and one of the solutions would be to have the &quot;Gnosis&quot; or the &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; or &quot;Avatar&quot; to whisper only in the heads of Hermetics and Choristers, and not in the heads of the Euthanatoi, Etherites or Technocrats.<br /> <br /> That way, hermetics could annoy everybody else non-stop about &quot;Avatars&quot; and claim that &quot;you closed yourself to true Divine Revelation&quot;, and then you could really flip a coin into whether his right or just mildly insane, and instead is just doing &quot;inspired science&quot; as his etherite colleage also annoyingly keeps saying.<br /> <br /> That however is not the game we have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:04:22-07:00","id":1516567,"title":"","content":"Again, that's more of a Disparates thing. The thing that sets the Traditions apart from the Disparates is that they <i>have</i> worked out a way to get along despite their differences, and not just because they share a common enemy. They're not all kumbayah about it; as both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> and I have said, they <i>do</i> have infighting. But an alliance doesn't last for over five hundred years without its members establishing some sort of common ground. <br /> <br /> And in the Traditions, that common ground is the idea that everyone's basically doing the same thing, in different ways. When an Akashayana looks at her Euthanatos companion, she sees someone whose way of doing things clashes with her own, so much so that for centuries before the founding of the Traditions, the two factions fought a bloody multigenerational war. But since then, they've buried the hatchet, and her attitude toward him is \u201cI don't understand how he can think the way he does; but he probably can't understand how I think either, so I should give him the benefit of the doubt.\u201d Or something like that. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:12:24-07:00","id":1516568,"title":"","content":"By the way, VtM and Demon the Fallen reforce the gnostic elements of the WoD, because those games give us the biggest gnostic element of all... The Demiurge.<br /> <br /> The &quot;God&quot; that curses Cain to vampirism isnt the God of the Bible after all...<br /> <br /> And the entire cosmology of WoD is theosophical. To begin with, it's an animist/totemist world; that's the hermetic/theosophical part (all religions are &quot;just one&quot;). Christians, muslims, buddhists, jews, hinduists, zoroastrians and many many more dont believe that every rock has a spirit. And yet, that's how the WoD is. The world of WoD is an illusion; that's the gnostic/hermetic stuff right there. The world is a fabrication of the &quot;Consensus&quot;. As per WtA &quot;matter and spirit were once one&quot;. The material plane is an illusion and a &quot;prison for the soul&quot;. Gnosticism. A great cataclysm separated matter and spirit for WtA. Akin to &quot;God (the real God) fragmented himself&quot; from Gnosticism. <br /> <br /> All games of WoD reinforce that. Changelling is the same, &quot;the Shattering&quot;. It's all a work of the evil Demiurge that set that terrible scourge of vampirism into the world and that trapped the &quot;good guys&quot; following Lucifer (the saint) into the Abyss. That's gnosticism 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:24:19-07:00","id":1516573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you are interpreting things into YOUR headcanon. But that's NOT how the books interpret things. In tne books, Avatars are REAL. Whatever their exact nature is.</div> </div> </div> </div>As are you, when you say that we should just ditch the Avatar mechanics. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, they are NOT just a &quot;source of magic(k)&quot;. They talk inside your head.<br /> <br /> And for them not to talk, you need a special trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you under the impression that because Circumspect Avatar is a Merit, that a Circumspect Avatar is somehow less of a genuine article than an unmodified Avatar? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, not all Techies get Circumspect Avatar. Many techies also get their &quot;Geniuses&quot; schizophrenic voice inside their heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that <i>all</i> Techies get a Circumspect Avatar. There are exceptions, just like there's the occasional Chorister who has a Circumspect Avatar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, those voices arent just schizophrenia, just phantom voices; they actually have VALUABLE information, sometimes the kind of which the Mage himself couldnt possibly have. So no, the game itself contradicts everything you're saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they talk. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatars are VERY real, and are the real thing. Sure, you can <b>personally interpret</b> them away, but that's not what the books say.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, there's nothing wrong with personal interpretations; you're doing it, too. Second, I do <i>not</i> deny that Avatars exist. I'm just saying that they aren't all chatterboxes; and the ones that aren't can be interpreted as \u201cmerely\u201d sources of Magick without decorating in any significant manner from the books. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Im not suggesting any headcanon, Im simply stating a fact that Mage has a heavily gnostic philosophy behind it, and if the purpose was to truly make it so that &quot;anything goes&quot;, than Hermeticism shouldnt be <b>The Truth</b> (because it is),</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you so far; and this is, in fact, my goal as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and one of the solutions would be to have the &quot;Gnosis&quot; or the &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; or &quot;Avatar&quot; to whisper only in the heads of Hermetics and Choristers, and not in the heads of the Euthanatoi, Etherites or Technocrats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fancy that: you just said <i>exactly the same thing I did,</i> differing only in terms of how to implement it. <br /> <br /> I have a feeling that we may be a lot closer to agreement than you might think we are. It's possible that we're arguing over a molehill. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516565#post1516565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That way, hermetics could annoy everybody else non-stop about &quot;Avatars&quot; and claim that &quot;you closed yourself to true Divine Revelation&quot;, and then you could really flip a coin into whether his right or just mildly insane, and instead is just doing &quot;inspired science&quot; as his etherite colleage also annoyingly keeps saying.<br /> <br /> That however is not the game we have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I stated that I was simply expressing my preferences, and not a literal reading of the rules. <br /> <br /> But in practical terms (i.e., how you choose to run the game), it <i>could</i> be. Just don't be so literal in your reading of the Avatar Background and the related Merits, and you're fine. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:36:18-07:00","id":1516575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516573#post1516573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As are you, when you say that we should just ditch the Avatar mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are you under the impression that because Circumspect Avatar is a Merit, that a Circumspect Avatar is somehow less of a genuine article than an unmodified Avatar?<br /> <br /> <br /> I never said that <i>all</i> Techies get a Circumspect Avatar. There are exceptions, just like there's the occasional Chorister who has a Circumspect Avatar.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only if they talk.<br /> <br /> <br /> First of all, there's nothing wrong with personal interpretations; you're doing it, too. Second, I do <i>not</i> deny that Avatars exist. I'm just saying that they aren't all chatterboxes; and the ones that aren't can be interpreted as \u201cmerely\u201d sources of Magick without decorating in any significant manner from the books.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm with you so far; and this is, in fact, my goal as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fancy that: you just said <i>exactly the same thing I did,</i> differing only in terms of how to implement it.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling that we may be a lot closer to agreement than you might think we are. It's possible that we're arguing over a molehill.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is why I stated that I was simply expressing my preferences, and not a literal reading of the rules.<br /> <br /> But in practical terms (i.e., how you choose to run the game), it <i>could</i> be. Just don't be so literal in your reading of the Avatar Background and the related Merits, and you're fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, were are arguing and disagreeing about the fact that we agree. What Im saying is that the world of WoD holds hermeticism/gnosticism as THE TRUTH, when the (alleged) purpose should be for it to be &quot;maybe, who knows&quot;.<br /> <br /> And what Im arguing is that the game absolutely have Avatars as a fact. No, your &quot;magic&quot; dont come from Gods, it doesnt come from spirits, it doesnt come from the psychic powers of your mind and it doesnt come from scientific principles. It comes from a fragment of THE Divine (not from &quot;a&quot; divine, but THE Divine - The One). Period.<br /> <br /> That's what the books say. Then, they do tons of mental gymnastics to justify why some groups think otherwise. Ok, some groups think differently - but those are just WRONG. Period.<br /> <br /> Now, we CAN overlook all of that and say &quot;you know what, the schizophrenic voices will only eco in the heads of the hermetics and choristers and no others&quot;. Sure, we can do that. And it might be an interesting solution.<br /> <br /> But it's a solution that goes outside of the entire game premisse. That's my point. That although we can more or less ignore Avatars, that goes against the game canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:37:43-07:00","id":1516577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516568#post1516568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, VtM and Demon the Fallen reforce the gnostic elements of the WoD, because those games give us the biggest gnostic element of all... The Demiurge.<br /> <br /> The &quot;God&quot; that curses Cain to vampirism isnt the God of the Bible after all...<br /> <br /> And the entire cosmology of WoD is theosophical. To begin with, it's an animist/totemist world; that's the hermetic/theosophical part (all religions are &quot;just one&quot;). Christians, muslims, buddhists, jews, hinduists, zoroastrians and many many more dont believe that every rock has a spirit. And yet, that's how the WoD is. The world of WoD is an illusion; that's the gnostic/hermetic stuff right there. The world is a fabrication of the &quot;Consensus&quot;. As per WtA &quot;matter and spirit were once one&quot;. The material plane is an illusion and a &quot;prison for the soul&quot;. Gnosticism. A great cataclysm separated matter and spirit for WtA. Akin to &quot;God (the real God) fragmented himself&quot; from Gnosticism.<br /> <br /> All games of WoD reinforce that. Changelling is the same, &quot;the Shattering&quot;. It's all a work of the evil Demiurge that set that terrible scourge of vampirism into the world and that trapped the &quot;good guys&quot; following Lucifer (the saint) into the Abyss. That's gnosticism 101.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Ascension</b> (the final book of the original run) had a section in it suggesting a Fractured Cosmos, where each gameline exists in its own universe, with its own metaphysics; but with a resonant effect that causes the events in the various parallel universes to rhyme. For instance, Awakened people in the Mage universe have counterparts in the Hunter universe that are Witches; and while there are no Garou in the Vampire universe, there <i>are</i> lupines, which are similar but not quite the same. <br /> <br /> This is a meta-concept, implementing in-setting the following idea: the World of Darkness isn't one thing; each <i>gameline</i> is its own thing, which is consistent with other gamelines in some ways and inconsistent with them in other ways. Trying to come up with a single, consistent cosmology that fits <i>every</i> gameline is an exercise in futility. <br /> <br /> And that's why, this being the Mage forum, I'm not going to discuss the Gnosticism that may or may not be present in the other gamelines: it's not relevant to a discussion about Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:46:31-07:00","id":1516578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516575#post1516575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, were are arguing and disagreeing about the fact that we agree. What Im saying is that the world of WoD holds hermeticism/gnosticism as THE TRUTH, when the (alleged) purpose should be for it to be &quot;maybe, who knows&quot;.<br /> <br /> And what Im arguing is that the game absolutely have Avatars as a fact. No, your &quot;magic&quot; dont come from Gods, it doesnt come from spirits, it doesnt come from the psychic powers of your mind and it doesnt come from scientific principles. It comes from a fragment of THE Divine (not from &quot;a&quot; divine, but THE Divine - The One). Period.<br /> <br /> That's what the books say. Then, they do tons of mental gymnastics to justify why some groups think otherwise. Ok, some groups think differently - but those are just WRONG. Period.<br /> <br /> Now, we CAN overlook all of that and say &quot;you know what, the schizophrenic voices will only eco in the heads of the hermetics and choristers and no others&quot;. Sure, we can do that. And it might be an interesting solution.<br /> <br /> But it's a solution that goes outside of the entire game premisse. That's my point. That although we can more or less ignore Avatars, that goes against the game canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what? There's something that Brucato has said several times, both in M20 and when talking about it: \u201cIt's Your Game; Do With It As You Will.\u201d <br /> <br /> M20 doesn't <i>have</i> a \u201ccanon\u201d; just the developer's preferred way of doing things. Which, by his own words, is no more valid than the gamers' preferences. <br /> <br /> <i>Especially</i> when the changes I make are deliberately <i>minimal</i>: I do my best to stay as close to the published material as I can while still effecting the differences that I'm after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:54:58-07:00","id":1516580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516575#post1516575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, were are arguing and disagreeing about the fact that we agree. What Im saying is that the world of WoD holds hermeticism/gnosticism as THE TRUTH, when the (alleged) purpose should be for it to be &quot;maybe, who knows&quot;.<br /> <br /> And what Im arguing is that the game absolutely have Avatars as a fact. No, your &quot;magic&quot; dont come from Gods, it doesnt come from spirits, it doesnt come from the psychic powers of your mind and it doesnt come from scientific principles. It comes from a fragment of THE Divine (not from &quot;a&quot; divine, but THE Divine - The One). Period.<br /> <br /> That's what the books say. Then, they do tons of mental gymnastics to justify why some groups think otherwise. Ok, some groups think differently - but those are just WRONG. Period.<br /> <br /> Now, we CAN overlook all of that and say &quot;you know what, the schizophrenic voices will only eco in the heads of the hermetics and choristers and no others&quot;. Sure, we can do that. And it might be an interesting solution.<br /> <br /> But it's a solution that goes outside of the entire game premisse. That's my point. That although we can more or less ignore Avatars, that goes against the game canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is saying that Avatars aren't a thing. But they are just that: a THING (without proper definition in raw) that awakens magick. That's it. Anything beyond that is your mage belief. Nowhere is said that they are spirits. NOWHERE is said that they *indeed are* part of The One and nowhere is said that they necessarily have to talk.<br /> <br /> in the end of the day, NO ONE knows for sure what an avatar is, because the books didn't say exactly what it is. This is left intentionally vague, just so it could fit any paradigm.<br /> <br /> If you can base your point with raw, I would appreciate, but I can't remember M20 giving FACTS about avatars other than: A) they exist and B) they awaken magick.<br /> <br /> You will find a lot of &quot;might&quot; be this or &quot;might&quot; be that and &quot;your mage believes&quot;, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:01:17-07:00","id":1516582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516561#post1516561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can only think that you are oversimplifying something that should be more complicated, the traditions look down on each other because they see their creeds as... eccentric, to say the least, I don't think all of them are capable of being so open-minded to the point where they respect each other, they only team up out of necessity and they kind of know what can happen if they don't, people do that and they find ways to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need <b>all</b> of them to be open minded. Of course there will be mages that conflict with others paradigms. But at their core, at their leaderships and most importantly, at their rules, they have to share this open mindness, if only dor things to work. <br /> <br /> They already do in the game scenario, in some ways, since the Traditions are a thing. They would just have to win the war and then organize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:03:08-07:00","id":1516584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516578#post1516578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what? There's something that Brucato has said several times, both in M20 and when talking about it: \u201cIt's Your Game; Do With It As You Will.\u201d<br /> <br /> M20 doesn't <i>have</i> a \u201ccanon\u201d; just the developer's preferred way of doing things. Which, by his own words, is no more valid than the gamers' preferences.<br /> <br /> <i>Especially</i> when the changes I make are deliberately <i>minimal</i>: I do my best to stay as close to the published material as I can while still effecting the differences that I'm after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not arguing that. Of course you can do as you please. You could play MtA on the D&amp;D realm of Ravenloft or in the world of Shadowrun that has an ancient dragon as the president of the United States. You could do any of that, but that has never been my point. Im not telling you &quot;no no no, you cant circumspect all the &quot;avatars&quot; of the techies! That's not what the holy text says!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Im not saying that. Of course you change things as you best see fit, I do it all the time.<br /> <br /> The argument begun when I claimed that the WoD <b>as written</b> is definitely hermeticist/gnostic, thus making the OoH the &quot;right ones&quot;. And several people disagreed, and I showed my reasons as to why I believe that to be the case. That's why Im being so adamant about it. Because, as written, technocrats are self deluded idiots, Dreamspeakers were also delusional thinking their magic came from &quot;the spirits&quot; (lol savages) and etherites are mad idiots and so on... Only the hermetics, choristers and ahl-i-batin actually got their shit togheter, all the rest are just dumb fools.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly why I myself change so much in my games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:16:11-07:00","id":1516588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516584#post1516584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument begun when I claimed that the WoD <b>as written</b> is definitely hermeticist/gnostic, thus making the OoH the &quot;right ones&quot;. And several people disagreed, and I showed my reasons as to why I believe that to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div> Right. But I'm not one of them. I have never said that I disagree with your assertion about Gnosticism. Since it first came up, I've been focusing entirely on <i>what to do about it.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516584#post1516584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why Im being so adamant about it. Because, as written, technocrats are self deluded idiots,</div> </div> </div> </div>I call this the \u201call liars or dupes\u201d problem; and it's precisely this that got me going on the, to use your phrasing, \u201cGnosticism isn't The Truth; it's just another paradigm believed by some and not by others\u201d thing. With that established, the next question is \u201cwhat's the smallest set of changes needed to make this so?\u201d<br /> <br /> Perhaps you should save your outrage for someone who has actually voiced disagreement with you about what Mage actually says?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:32:24-07:00","id":1516592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516580#post1516580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one is saying that Avatars aren't a thing. But they are just that: a THING (without proper definition in raw) that awakens magick. That's it. Anything beyond that is your mage belief. Nowhere is said that they are spirits. NOWHERE is said that they *indeed are* part of The One and nowhere is said that they necessarily have to talk.<br /> <br /> in the end of the day, NO ONE knows for sure what an avatar is, because the books didn't say exactly what it is. This is left intentionally vague, just so it could fit any paradigm.<br /> <br /> If you can base your point with raw, I would appreciate, but I can't remember M20 giving FACTS about avatars other than: A) they exist and B) they awaken magick.<br /> <br /> You will find a lot of &quot;might&quot; be this or &quot;might&quot; be that and &quot;your mage believes&quot;, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, too bad that they talk to you. And sometimes appear for you. And that all the game mechanics use them as a concept. And that only human beings have them - despite there being other kinds of magic critters out there (vamps, weres, fae and more)<br /> <br /> You have the &quot;Avatar Background&quot;. Not &quot;Magic(k) Potency&quot; or &quot;Mojo Power&quot; backgrounds. No. Avatar. Ok, the self deluded idiots on the other side call it &quot;Genius&quot;, but we know they're idiots, and this is just Avatar with a fancy technobabble name, just like &quot;Dimensional Science&quot;. Scream all you want about &quot;oh, it's all paradigm&quot;, but we all know that the technocrats are NOT exploring &quot;parallel dimensions&quot;, they are venturing into the SPIRIT WORLD. Period.<br /> <br /> You can, like I already said, buy into the fluffy, and that's the thing, there's what the books say in a &quot;sort of&quot; &quot;out and in character&quot;. So yeah, when the books say &quot;oh yes, we techies have geniuses!&quot;, that's sort of &quot;in character&quot;. But when it tells you &quot;that's your Avatar background rating&quot;, that's the out of character explanation of how it TRULY works.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, each Tradition believes in their own sets of spheres&quot;. Yeah right, now shut up and try to combine Life and Matter to do &quot;Necromancy&quot; mister Euthanathoi...<br /> <br /> Also, I dont remember exactly every world from M20, but 2ed and rev made all these concepts very clear. Avatar is a thing. Period. It's not your soul, it's connected to your soul but it's something else... And that part was a bit vague, but what was NOT vague is that the Avatar is not just some sort &quot;psychic ability&quot;, and that it is DEFINITELY connected to the &quot;soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the raw for that is abundant and more than self evident, but I have a feeling that you are personally hanging out on the propaganda of &quot;oh, it's a game where it's all subjective and any answer could be right&quot;. It's not.<br /> <br /> So, so begin with: Gilgul.<br /> <br /> How do you destroy the source of &quot;Magic(k)&quot; from any Mage?<br /> <br /> Oh yes, that's right. You do it by using Spirit 5. Also know (until Rev ed at least) as &quot;Touch Avatars&quot; suggestive name for an effect that deals with this exotic &quot;thing&quot; that may or may not be connected to the &quot;soul&quot;, and yet you need mastery over SPIRIT to deal with it - not Mind, as would perhaps be the case if this &quot;thing&quot; were just some &quot;psychic resonance power&quot;, not Prime if it were the case that it is some &quot;meta-magic&quot; thing. Not Entropy, in case it were the &quot;Power of Destiny&quot;.<br /> <br /> No. It's spirit.<br /> <br /> And second: a background called &quot;Avatar&quot; is not the most indicative of their nature.<br /> <br /> What's much more indicative is the many traits about PAST LIVES.<br /> <br /> Right there it all ends. People reincarnate (or at least, the awaken elite with &quot;Gnosis&quot; does. The peasantry is anybody's guess).<br /> <br /> So no, the &quot;Avatar&quot; isnt just some magic energy of the world pf the fairies that randomly &quot;parasite&quot; Mages granting them superpowers. Its DEFINETELY part of the human soul, even if the &quot;soul&quot; may have additional components.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T20:06:44-07:00","id":1516598,"title":"","content":"Reencarnation in fact proves how the techies are a bunch of self deluded idiots. And it proves my point that, just because some group believes in something, it doesnt mean anything. The techies DONT believe in reencarnation, but it is a FACT. And the reason why it is a fact <b>beyond any doubt</b> and not just some &quot;oh, I believe&quot; thing and why the &quot;Past Lives&quot; background aint just bad acid trip is because there are OFFICIAL characters who have reencarnated. I can remember of at least one, Amanda, a disciple of Senex, and the reason why there's no doubt she DEFINITELY reencarnated is because Senex was the one that killed her past life (because she turned Nefandus), and he also &quot;fixed&quot; her Avatar in her new encarnation - or at least &quot;blocked&quot; it in some way to avoid letting her corrupted Avatar to turn her into a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> So, there you have it. Technocrats are idiots that believe in clearly untrue ideas that do NOT correspond to the true functioning of the world.<br /> <br /> Now, it can be said that INSIDE THE WORLD they can reasonably make such an assumption, but for us, looking OUTSIDE OF THEIR WORLD as the Gods that we are, we cant possibly fall to the same lies.<br /> <br /> The technocrats are wrong, as are the Etherites, the Euthanathoi and many others; the hermetics are right. End of story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T20:45:26-07:00","id":1516605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom#post1515686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason the Technocracy use to control the world and the Consensus, is safety. (...)<br /> Downtown has a rating of 8. Which is the same as a busy market place in DA.<br /> (...) all that changed was +1 in rating in Gauntlet? <br /> So, is this safety thing only Technocratic propaganda<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to efforts and choices of various Technocrats ( and other Mage organizations, factions, nations, guilds, and groups - like the Technepandi, Society of the Ether, and Virtual Adepts ) mundane humans ( who are also called mortals, or normal humans ) by default and initially support clearly scientific decisions and investments, and particularly social network and family oriented goals and achievements, and also as well viewpoints, schemes, plans, and values that are definitely intelectual, This means that some of supernatural beings might find it harder or different to realize thei advancements and goals, and that they might very well need to suceed and develop crafts, philosophies, and resources differently. <br /> <br /> This is not neccesarily directly because of mystical methods, otherwordly abilities, or magical ideas of the various mysticism, occult, spiritualism, magic, nature, and religion oriented teams and groups. I think that in regard to the possible interactions, impact, possibilities, and influence that many Technocrats ( for example from the Syndicate Convention, or from the NWO Convention ) have and develop ( in regard to these magical, otherwordly, occult, and mystical tendencies, events, emotions, values, and qualities ) what matters and is important is the preference, the ease, the variety, and the support for and in regard to systematic, analytic, scientific, predictable, and scientific methods, attitudes, notions, concepts, tools, and capabilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will mention here some of these groups. They are definitely and clearly interesting and noteworthy in regard to their various unique facts, traits, strenghts, or qualities in their particular capacities as guilds, chapters, organizations, and teams. the Council of the Nine Mystical Traditions ( just to mention three of tthe Traditions : the Order of Hermes, the Verbenae, and the Celestial Choir ) or the Uktena Garou, or the Grandfather Thunder's Shadow Lords Tribe, or the Silver Fangs Falcon's Tribe, or the Nephandi,<br /> <br /> It is vital, key, and important to underline and mention that these to at least some extent these groups very often and commonly have at least some personal and important stake, attachement, and interest in machinery, tinkering, information, invetions, gadgets, safety, knowledge, mathematics, transportation, architecture, ecology, modernization, and technology. These ideas, goals, concepts, ambitions, and notions can very well be comparable to the attitudes, tendencies, values, and decisions of Technocrats ( for example from the Syndicate Convention, or the Iteration-X Convention ) However I do consider that these machinery, information, and technology oriented attitudes and goals are definitely separate, additional, and also to some considerable or meaningful extent secondary or supplementary to the different and varied heroic, mystical, spiritual, legendary, mythical, and religious leanings, tendecies, values, emotions, plans, and ambitions. <br /> <br /> <br /> It is visible, clear, and definite that due to actions of Sympathizers, Extraordianry Citizens, and Technocrats ( and also of course various additional friends and allies ) there are many attractive and developed scientific and technological attitudes, capabilities, approaches, philosophies, ideas, notions, methods, schemes, and values ; that are definitely understandable, accesible, and supported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T21:08:56-07:00","id":1516607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516598#post1516598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reencarnation in fact proves how the techies are a bunch of self deluded idiots. And it proves my point that, just because some group believes in something, it doesnt mean anything. The techies DONT believe in reencarnation, but it is a FACT. And the reason why it is a fact <b>beyond any doubt</b> and not just some &quot;oh, I believe&quot; thing and why the &quot;Past Lives&quot; background aint just bad acid trip is because there are OFFICIAL characters who have reencarnated. I can remember of at least one, Amanda, a disciple of Senex, and the reason why there's no doubt she DEFINITELY reencarnated is because Senex was the one that killed her past life (because she turned Nefandus), and he also &quot;fixed&quot; her Avatar in her new encarnation - or at least &quot;blocked&quot; it in some way to avoid letting her corrupted Avatar to turn her into a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> So, there you have it. Technocrats are idiots that believe in clearly untrue ideas that do NOT correspond to the true functioning of the world.<br /> <br /> Now, it can be said that INSIDE THE WORLD they can reasonably make such an assumption, but for us, looking OUTSIDE OF THEIR WORLD as the Gods that we are, we cant possibly fall to the same lies.<br /> <br /> The technocrats are wrong, as are the Etherites, the Euthanathoi and many others; the hermetics are right. End of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I don't see any way of hacking the game so that \u201creincarnation is real\u201d is just a belief, any more than the game can be hacked to say that \u201cspirits are real\u201d is just a belief. Likewise with \u201cAvatars are real\u201d.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe difference is that how your <i>own</i> Avatar is built can and should be closely associated with your Focus; and \u201cthe source of my own Magick\u201d isn't something that a mage should be demonstrably wrong about<b></b>: the likes of the technos <i>shouldn't</i> have Avatars that talk to them, as that interferes with their materialistic beliefs \u2014 with the odd exception to prove the rule, of course (which is addressed by the \u201cDemented Eidolon\u201d Flaw). <br /> <br /> Though frankly, something similar applies to reincarnation as well: it's one thing for a Techno to not believe in reincarnation as long as they haven't actually encountered someone who has demonstrably reincarnated; that's just ignorance, and can potentially apply to anyone. But if they themselves are reincarnated? That's a different matter. And incidentally, <i>that's</i> worth a <i>Merit</i> for Technocrats in the RAW: Inner Knight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T04:07:34-07:00","id":1516628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516607#post1516607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I don't see any way of hacking the game so that \u201creincarnation is real\u201d is just a belief, any more than the game can be hacked to say that \u201cspirits are real\u201d is just a belief. Likewise with \u201cAvatars are real\u201d.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe difference is that how your <i>own</i> Avatar is built can and should be closely associated with your Focus; and \u201cthe source of my own Magick\u201d isn't something that a mage should be demonstrably wrong about<b></b>: the likes of the technos <i>shouldn't</i> have Avatars that talk to them, as that interferes with their materialistic beliefs \u2014 with the odd exception to prove the rule, of course (which is addressed by the \u201cDemented Eidolon\u201d Flaw).<br /> <br /> Though frankly, something similar applies to reincarnation as well: it's one thing for a Techno to not believe in reincarnation as long as they haven't actually encountered someone who has demonstrably reincarnated; that's just ignorance, and can potentially apply to anyone. But if they themselves are reincarnated? That's a different matter. And incidentally, <i>that's</i> worth a <i>Merit</i> for Technocrats in the RAW: Inner Knight.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one way, but not many people would like that...<br /> <br /> And that is... The technocrats are lying...<br /> <br /> I do like that approach thou, but it dramatically changes the setting. It turns the Union into a powerful Cabala of &quot;hermetic&quot; wizards that uses technology as a curtain under the world, a simple control mechanism, and to them a convenience rather than a necessity. <br /> <br /> I understand why many wouldnt like this, but in my opinion it would make them even more Machiavellian, since gone would be any assumptions that they fight for what they believe in a sense - their only creed would be exactly that - &quot;safety above freedom&quot;, and they would be unapologetic about it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, in the world we created it is harder for people to awaken and ascend, but at least the peasants are fed and protected&quot;. And they would have an adamant iron fist about that vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T05:26:17-07:00","id":1516635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516598#post1516598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reencarnation in fact proves how the techies are a bunch of self deluded idiots. And it proves my point that, just because some group believes in something, it doesnt mean anything. The techies DONT believe in reencarnation, but it is a FACT. And the reason why it is a fact <b>beyond any doubt</b> and not just some &quot;oh, I believe&quot; thing and why the &quot;Past Lives&quot; background aint just bad acid trip is because there are OFFICIAL characters who have reencarnated. I can remember of at least one, Amanda, a disciple of Senex, and the reason why there's no doubt she DEFINITELY reencarnated is because Senex was the one that killed her past life (because she turned Nefandus), and he also &quot;fixed&quot; her Avatar in her new encarnation - or at least &quot;blocked&quot; it in some way to avoid letting her corrupted Avatar to turn her into a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> So, there you have it. Technocrats are idiots that believe in clearly untrue ideas that do NOT correspond to the true functioning of the world.<br /> <br /> Now, it can be said that INSIDE THE WORLD they can reasonably make such an assumption, but for us, looking OUTSIDE OF THEIR WORLD as the Gods that we are, we cant possibly fall to the same lies.<br /> <br /> The technocrats are wrong, as are the Etherites, the Euthanathoi and many others; the hermetics are right. End of story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ah, this sounds familiar. These kinds of discussions happen from time to time and there\u2019s something we should cover before we go any further:<br /> <br /> Mage contradicts itself all the time.<br /> <br /> <i>All the time.</i><br /> <br /> Name a single issue that you think is core to what Mage is and you can find statements, rules, and other writings that call it into dispute. In fact, you can usually find someone on these forums ready to deny that it is core to Mage and to bring quotes to the table to prove it. For instance, quite a few people read Mage and get the idea that it is the Technocracy that works closer the metaphysical truths of reality. And they can point to places in the books that seem to agree.<br /> <br /> Through a combination of bugs and features, Mage is a game of contradictory truths, and while that can cause problems it also resonates well with a game about fighting over reality and truth.<br /> <br /> So yes, there are gnostic elements in some of the Traditions (some intentional, some only because of passing resemblance) that doesn't mean that gnosticism is baked into the game, intentionally or otherwise.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T06:54:13-07:00","id":1516640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516592#post1516592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, too bad that they talk to you. And sometimes appear for you. And that all the game mechanics use them as a concept. And that only human beings have them - despite there being other kinds of magic critters out there (vamps, weres, fae and more)<br /> <br /> You have the &quot;Avatar Background&quot;. Not &quot;Magic(k) Potency&quot; or &quot;Mojo Power&quot; backgrounds. No. Avatar. Ok, the self deluded idiots on the other side call it &quot;Genius&quot;, but we know they're idiots, and this is just Avatar with a fancy technobabble name, just like &quot;Dimensional Science&quot;. Scream all you want about &quot;oh, it's all paradigm&quot;, but we all know that the technocrats are NOT exploring &quot;parallel dimensions&quot;, they are venturing into the SPIRIT WORLD. Period.<br /> <br /> You can, like I already said, buy into the fluffy, and that's the thing, there's what the books say in a &quot;sort of&quot; &quot;out and in character&quot;. So yeah, when the books say &quot;oh yes, we techies have geniuses!&quot;, that's sort of &quot;in character&quot;. But when it tells you &quot;that's your Avatar background rating&quot;, that's the out of character explanation of how it TRULY works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you provide a print or a page number for the exact raw about those claims? And I don't mean &quot;they might&quot; stuff. I mean a sentence saying that Avatars *are* definitely spirits or they necessarily *have* to talk to the mage. I will wait for your answer.<br /> <br /> So, you are trying to make a point based on the name &quot;Avatar&quot;? Did you want that every single time the book says &quot;Avatar&quot;, it said &quot;Avatar/Genius&quot;? Sorry, the book using the word Avatar is no proof that the Tradition view of Avatar is more true than a techno view. It's just a w\u200b<br /> <br /> You are having a really hard time to differentiate in-game and out-of-game. In-game, Avatars/Genius are what the mage believes they are. Out of game, WE DON'T HAVE A CONCRET DEFINITION FOR IT. If they did that, please show me the page in M20. And if the concept is left vague this way, Technos *could* be right. That's my point.<br /> <br /> All your arguments about Techs lying are exactly what a Tradition mage would argue in-game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516592#post1516592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Oh, each Tradition believes in their own sets of spheres&quot;. Yeah right, now shut up and try to combine Life and Matter to do &quot;Necromancy&quot; mister Euthanathoi...</div> </div> </div> </div>I never made a point about spheres. Yeah, out of game Spheres are a thing. The Hermetics area right on this one. Although, several Traditions (and I believe Crats too) do classify magick similarly as spheres.<br /> <br /> And to be honest here, there are another thing that Traditions are &quot;more&quot; right than Crats (or technos in general): the belief on the internal power of the mage instead of an external one. Technomancers believe their machines are the source of their power, while mystics believe their power come from themselves. Out of game, the mystics are right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516592#post1516592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I dont remember exactly every world from M20, but 2ed and rev made all these concepts very clear. Avatar is a thing. Period. It's not your soul, it's connected to your soul but it's something else... And that part was a bit vague, but what was NOT vague is that the Avatar is not just some sort &quot;psychic ability&quot;, and that it is DEFINITELY connected to the &quot;soul&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the raw for that is abundant and more than self evident, but I have a feeling that you are personally hanging out on the propaganda of &quot;oh, it's a game where it's all subjective and any answer could be right&quot;. It's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. I know Avatars is a thing. I'm not discussing that. I'm discussing its out of game definitions and who (sect) is right.<br /> <br /> What is a soul? Lol, we don't even have a definition for that, both in and out of game. Much less the definition of an Avatar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516592#post1516592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. It's spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you are stuck with names. The Sphere Spirit is called Dimensional Science. In game, hermetics believe that spirits are spirits. Crats believe spirits are beings of another dimension. Out of game we call them spirits for a lack of better word.<br /> <br /> Tell me, exactly what is the difference between a spirit and another dimension being?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: And lastly, what does all that has to do with safety vs. freedom? lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T10:16:35-07:00","id":1516669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516635#post1516635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ah, this sounds familiar. These kinds of discussions happen from time to time and there\u2019s something we should cover before we go any further:<br /> <br /> Mage contradicts itself all the time.<br /> <br /> <i>All the time.</i><br /> <br /> Name a single issue that you think is core to what Mage is and you can find statements, rules, and other writings that call it into dispute. In fact, you can usually find someone on these forums ready to deny that it is core to Mage and to bring quotes to the table to prove it. For instance, quite a few people read Mage and get the idea that it is the Technocracy that works closer the metaphysical truths of reality. And they can point to places in the books that seem to agree.<br /> <br /> Through a combination of bugs and features, Mage is a game of contradictory truths, and while that can cause problems it also resonates well with a game about fighting over reality and truth.<br /> <br /> So yes, there are gnostic elements in some of the Traditions (some intentional, some only because of passing resemblance) that doesn't mean that gnosticism is baked into the game, intentionally or otherwise.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I could agree with you. On some things.<br /> <br /> On others, I cannot. Reencarnation is a thing. It's an undisputed fact - even for technocrats (including rules about it).<br /> <br /> Technocrats still need &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; 5 in order to genengineer a &quot;real&quot; human being. Not just Mind and Life 5 - and they know it. They know that true consciousness lies outside of the matter - what the mystics call &quot;soul&quot; and the techies &quot;anthropic field&quot; (just more technobabble), but in the end of the day, the evidence points out against any sort of materialistic viewpoints in this case.<br /> <br /> It doesnt matter how much you believe you have &quot;psychic abilities&quot;, your &quot;powers&quot; wont be removed by the use of Mind, but by the use of either Spirit or Dimensional Science. <br /> <br /> There's no subjectivity in this point. Those are the realities and core aspects in the game. If you're a techie that dont believe in reencarnation, you're just flat out mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T11:05:24-07:00","id":1516672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516640#post1516640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you provide a print or a page number for the exact raw about those claims? And I don't mean &quot;they might&quot; stuff. I mean a sentence saying that Avatars *are* definitely spirits or they necessarily *have* to talk to the mage. I will wait for your answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont you worry, I will, as soon as time allows it. For that you can rest sure. I'll give you all the full quotes, the exact pages and the exact editions from which those quotes were taken from, you need not worry about that. I just wont give you quotes from the 1ed because I dont have it, but I bought the 2ed and Rev and M20, so you do not need to stress about it, those quotes will come, as soon as I have the time.<br /> <br /> Also, I never said that they HAVE to talk to the Mage (Circumspected Avatar is exactly for that); I said that some do, and that is enough for the point I'm making. You dont need every single Avatar/Genius to keep yapping non stop at every Mage's minds, but just the fact that SOME DO is already enough to prove that they are some sort of entity that is external to the Mage's own mind, particularly because they convey information from time to time that the Mage himself couldnt possibly know - again, it's not necessary that every single Avatar/Genius always act like a mysterious Oracle, but just the fact that this does happen already proves my point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, you are trying to make a point based on the name &quot;Avatar&quot;? Did you want that every single time the book says &quot;Avatar&quot;, it said &quot;Avatar/Genius&quot;? Sorry, the book using the word Avatar is no proof that the Tradition view of Avatar is more true than a techno view. It's just a w\u200b </div> </div> </div>That was not my point at all. You're creating a Straw Man in order to discuss semantics, rather than what my argument was.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are having a really hard time to differentiate in-game and out-of-game. In-game, Avatars/Genius are what the mage believes they are. Out of game, WE DON'T HAVE A CONCRET DEFINITION FOR IT. If they did that, please show me the page in M20. And if the concept is left vague this way, Technos *could* be right. That's my point. </div> </div> </div>We dont need a concrete definition of it, as long as we know what they ARE NOT.<br /> <br /> And what we know is that they are not just the result of a &quot;brilliant and rational mind&quot;. Any sleeper can be a &quot;genius&quot; with lower &quot;g&quot; and still not have an &quot;Enlightened Genius&quot; with big &quot;G&quot;. We know that an &quot;Enlightened Genius&quot; is not just a matter of a simple &quot;Eureka!&quot; moment.<br /> <br /> And the reason why we know it is because those &quot;Eurekas!&quot; can talk to the &quot;Scientist&quot; - again, let me be crystal clear this time so you dont resort to semantics once more in order to Straw Man my points: they CAN talk, they DO talk with some techies, from time to time, eventually, and more or less with each individual. It doesnt mean they are endlessly yapping on EVERY single Awaken/Enlightened mind all the time.<br /> <br /> Are we clear now? Good, so now we can stop diverting the argument. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All your arguments about Techs lying are exactly what a Tradition mage would argue in-game. </div> </div> </div>That was your most blatant Straw Man so far, so much so that I no longer believe you're discussing in good faith. <br /> <br /> At no moment I said the techies are lying. I said that it could be AN INTERESTING <b>DIFFERENT</b> PERPECTIVE for the game if they did.<br /> <br /> Im sorry, but after this one I can only imagine that you are maliciously trying to distort my words. For what reason, I do not know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to be honest here, there are another thing that Traditions are &quot;more&quot; right than Crats (or technos in general): the belief on the internal power of the mage instead of an external one. Technomancers believe their machines are the source of their power, while mystics believe their power come from themselves. Out of game, the mystics are right. </div> </div> </div>And with that, I won the entire argument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> At work now, rest I answer later<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T11:41:31-07:00","id":1516675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516669#post1516669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could agree with you. On some things.<br /> <br /> On others, I cannot. Reencarnation is a thing. It's an undisputed fact - even for technocrats (including rules about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are records of reincarnation but it is really ambiguous what is happening. Reincarnation of the Avatar? Reincarnation of the soul? Reincarnation of something else? Are they really reincarnating? Are they just tapping into the memories of someone else imprinted in the Umbra or in the Collective Consciousness? Something else?<br /> The ambiguity leaves plenty of room for debate in universe.<br /> <br /> Also, the two most Thesophical Traditions (the Chorus and Akashics) vehemently disagree on this issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technocrats still need &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; 5 in order to genengineer a &quot;real&quot; human being. Not just Mind and Life 5 - and they know it. They know that true consciousness lies outside of the matter - what the mystics call &quot;soul&quot; and the techies &quot;anthropic field&quot; (just more technobabble), but in the end of the day, the evidence points out against any sort of materialistic viewpoints in this case. </div> </div> </div>Sure, that\u2019s the sphere requirements as a game mechanic. Let\u2019s not fall into the old trap of assuming the game mechanics are the actual metaphysics of the world though.<br /> <br /> The Spheres, in game, are a common parlance meant to aid in communication, not an explanation for how all magic works. Some in the Disparates refuse to even use them. I\u2019d go so far as to say most Mages only use them for communication and otherwise think of magic entirely in terms of their own practices. If specific fields like the names of angels or quantum physics get arbitrarily divided up between \u201cspheres,\u201d well that\u2019s just an artifact of a clunky communication system.<br /> <br /> So no, I don\u2019t think that even materialist Technocrats (because they aren\u2019t all materialist) find it particularly meaningful that creating a person requires esoteric knowledge that is more commonly associated with dimensional science.<br /> <br /> For a real world example, there\u2019s a piece of math that covers both how Chernobyl went critical and why you have to steer bikes in the opposite direction when you turn sharply. That doesn\u2019t raise eyebrows or point to some hidden metaphysical connection between bicycles and nuclear power.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T12:21:03-07:00","id":1516679,"title":"","content":"Let me point out that Techies have to acknowledge that Magick is real (unless they're in Denial). They can say that it's something distinct from Science, and that its intent chaotic nature makes it dangerous and something to be contained or eliminated. But they can't deny that it <i>exists</i>. <br /> <br /> And that has consequences. Ghosts are real, which means that a worldview that says that intelligence is \u201cmerely\u201d an emergent property of sufficiently complex and structured matter is wrong. Reincarnation may be part of that Magick that Enlightened Scientists detest; but it's still definitely a thing, unless you're going to retreat into Denial. You cannot, therefore, seriously espouse a purely materialistic view of reality, message reality is demonstrably not materialistic. The closest you can come to that is to separate reality into Science and Magick and say that Science is materialistic but Magick isn't. And that has its own problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T12:32:03-07:00","id":1516680,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> It was not my intention to create any strawman. If they were, its was because I didn't understood your point.<br /> <br /> My initial discussion with you began with the &quot;mage setting is that gnostics are right &quot; argument. That I disagree.<br /> <br /> But we both agree that Avatars (or Genius, but you made clear the semantics is not in discussion.Good.) do exist.<br /> That spheres exists in-game and that mystics paradigms are closer to the real setting true than technomancers. This was not what I was discussing.<br /> <br /> Having said that, what makes you think that an Avatar couldn't be the mage's own consciousness, own subconscious talking to him? Where is it said that it *has* to be a spirit? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At no moment I said the techies are lying. I said that it could be AN INTERESTING DIFFERENT PERPECTIVE for the game if they did. </div> </div> </div>You said that Mage setting is gnostic and the Technocrats are wrong, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T04:08:08-07:00","id":1516753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516675#post1516675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, there are records of reincarnation but it is really ambiguous what is happening. Reincarnation of the Avatar? Reincarnation of the soul? Reincarnation of something else? Are they really reincarnating? Are they just tapping into the memories of someone else imprinted in the Umbra or in the Collective Consciousness? Something else?<br /> The ambiguity leaves plenty of room for debate in universe.<br /> <br /> Also, the two most Thesophical Traditions (the Chorus and Akashics) vehemently disagree on this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, I'll give you that. &quot;Reincarnated&quot; confirmed cases could indeed be people that weird cases of &quot;memory transfer&quot; naturally occurring through the Ether, or other such.<br /> <br /> That however wouldnt be the way a scientist in the real world would think; applying Occam's Razor to eliminate the unnecessary complexities... Or at least, the scientist would consider both hypotheses to be equally unlikely, thus neither could be discarded. <br /> <br /> Thus, actively believing in the <b>absence</b> of reincarnation (because that's what techies do, rather than disbelieving it) is DOGMA. But that's another conversation entirely. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, that\u2019s the sphere requirements as a game mechanic. Let\u2019s not fall into the old trap of assuming the game mechanics are the actual metaphysics of the world though.<br /> <br /> The Spheres, in game, are a common parlance meant to aid in communication, not an explanation for how all magic works. Some in the Disparates refuse to even use them. I\u2019d go so far as to say most Mages only use them for communication and otherwise think of magic entirely in terms of their own practices. If specific fields like the names of angels or quantum physics get arbitrarily divided up between \u201cspheres,\u201d well that\u2019s just an artifact of a clunky communication system.<br /> <br /> So no, I don\u2019t think that even materialist Technocrats (because they aren\u2019t all materialist) find it particularly meaningful that creating a person requires esoteric knowledge that is more commonly associated with dimensional science.<br /> <br /> For a real world example, there\u2019s a piece of math that covers both how Chernobyl went critical and why you have to steer bikes in the opposite direction when you turn sharply. That doesn\u2019t raise eyebrows or point to some hidden metaphysical connection between bicycles and nuclear power.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Fractals geometry. Yes, it's a fascinating subject. There's a mathematical correlation between the stock exchange, the populational cycles of organisms, formation of clouds, the leafs of a plant and pretty much any other &quot;random&quot; distributions over nature or human society alike.<br /> <br /> Sure, those things are not mystically connected (or maybe they are? I dont know. Im a skeptical materialist atheist, but Im not a God, thus I have to say that I may be wrong in my beliefs. Maybe there is a God... Quantum Physics may indicate that the universe operates like a super computer, constantly exchanging information so... Or maybe, all those fractals are the result of the &quot;algorithms&quot; and we are living in the matrix. Or maybe it's just a &quot;universal geometrical symmetry&quot;, born out of the simple fact that fractals are mathmatically easier to be formed. I dont know either way).<br /> <br /> However, in order to understand fractals, you have to learn arithmetic, then you learn algebra, geometry, trigonometry and calculus... You dont get your first class of math ever to be Fractals Geometry.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, for as much as people say that &quot;it's just mechanics&quot;, that's NOT TRUE.<br /> <br /> Because you could say &quot;I have a necromancer that dont adhere to the hermetic system&quot;. Ok, cool, but you wont be able to build one that knows how to &quot;Detect Undead, Turn Undead, Control Undead, Transform Undead and Shapeshift Undead&quot; AND NOTHING ELSE.<br /> <br /> Because you need the &quot;just mechanics that has nothing to do with the setting at all&quot; of the Spheres: Spirit, Matter, Life and maybe also Entropy and Prime.<br /> <br /> Meaning that, besides being able to fuse a pile of bodies into a &quot;Dragon Lich&quot; with &quot;Necromancy 5&quot;, you'll also be able to create &quot;Adamantium&quot; or &quot;Mithril&quot; with Matter 5, you'll be able to commune with the spirits of the forest with Spirit, and many other &quot;non-necrom-esque&quot; activities.<br /> <br /> I really wish that wasnt the case, but it is. Game mechanics dictates the setting in sense, so they should be built to fit into it rather they just having a label of &quot;ignore those when convenient&quot;.<br /> <br /> Game mechanics are like the &quot;laws of physics&quot; of the real world. We cant say that &quot;gravity is just the game mechanics of our simulation matrix&quot;. If you have broken game mechanics, the setting wont make sense.<br /> <br /> For instance, in the game &quot;Looney tunes&quot;, damage dont really hurts. If you KO an enemy, they spend an amount of rounds seeing starts around their heads, until they recover. That's the game mechanics about setting that is about doing funny stunts and nobody ever gets hurt, even when they are run out by a train.<br /> <br /> Imagine applying those same game mechanics to WoD and saying &quot;it's just game mechanics&quot;. The world wouldnt make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T04:21:26-07:00","id":1516755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516680#post1516680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> It was not my intention to create any strawman. If they were, its was because I didn't understood your point.<br /> <br /> My initial discussion with you began with the &quot;mage setting is that gnostics are right &quot; argument. That I disagree.<br /> <br /> But we both agree that Avatars (or Genius, but you made clear the semantics is not in discussion.Good.) do exist.<br /> That spheres exists in-game and that mystics paradigms are closer to the real setting true than technomancers. This was not what I was discussing.<br /> <br /> Having said that, what makes you think that an Avatar couldn't be the mage's own consciousness, own subconscious talking to him? Where is it said that it *has* to be a spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You said that Mage setting is gnostic and the Technocrats are wrong, right? </div> </div> </div>That doesnt mean they are automatically lying. I do make the case that it would be an interesting game if they actually were lying, that would make them to be much more of a Cabal of powerful individuals, much more like the ideas from the conspiracy theories about the &quot;Illuminatis&quot; and such. I think it would be highly interesting, but in this case they would just be a bunch of <b>hermetic</b> technomancers, disguising their arcane sorcery with the use of mechanic toys.<br /> <br /> That would be an interesting game, but very different from MtA.<br /> <br /> In fact, Gurps has this exact game: <b>The Cabal</b>. It's a cool one too, and much much more &quot;paranoid conspiracy theory&quot; than MtA.<br /> <br /> The other option for them is that they are simply WRONG. And hey, it happens. Somebody's gotta be wrong after all, and despite the claim of 100% subjectivity, that's not true. Marauders do get ejected from reality after all, and their views are obviously wrong.<br /> <br /> Also, are Nephandi also right? Maybe, but nephandi and non-nephandi cant possibly be both right at the same time.<br /> <br /> That's the thing, every single mage in the world cant possibly be all right at the same time. They could all be wrong thou... But despite the claims of the game, there IS some <b>objective truth</b>, even if we dont know what it is.<br /> <br /> If the Techies are right (I dont think so but ok), the Trads are wrong, and vice versa. Or both could be wrong.<br /> <br /> But MtA aint a solipsistic illusion built for each sole individual. <br /> <br /> (Late for work, answer more later, bye)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T05:34:32-07:00","id":1516761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516753#post1516753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I'll give you that. &quot;Reincarnated&quot; confirmed cases could indeed be people that weird cases of &quot;memory transfer&quot; naturally occurring through the Ether, or other such.<br /> <br /> That however wouldnt be the way a scientist in the real world would think; applying Occam's Razor to eliminate the unnecessary complexities... Or at least, the scientist would consider both hypotheses to be equally unlikely, thus neither could be discarded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Occam's razor doesn't discard hypotheses anyways. It often gets quoted as meaning that the simplest explanation is usually correct, but what it actually means is that the simplest explanation to disprove is the most efficient starting point. It's not a tool for finding truth, it is a tool for prioritizing effort. The conflation comes because when disproving a theory you generally start by assuming it is true and looking for contradictions. So in one sense the razor does say consider the simplest explanation is true, but it doesn't stop there. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fractals geometry. Yes, it's a fascinating subject. There's a mathematical correlation between the stock exchange, the populational cycles of organisms, formation of clouds, the leafs of a plant and pretty much any other &quot;random&quot; distributions over nature or human society alike. </div> </div> </div>Actually I was talking about control theory and positive plane poles. Its a way of determining system instability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately, for as much as people say that &quot;it's just mechanics&quot;, that's NOT TRUE.<br /> <br /> Because you could say &quot;I have a necromancer that dont adhere to the hermetic system&quot;. Ok, cool, but you wont be able to build one that knows how to &quot;Detect Undead, Turn Undead, Control Undead, Transform Undead and Shapeshift Undead&quot; AND NOTHING ELSE.<br /> <br /> Because you need the &quot;just mechanics that has nothing to do with the setting at all&quot; of the Spheres: Spirit, Matter, Life and maybe also Entropy and Prime.<br /> <br /> Meaning that, besides being able to fuse a pile of bodies into a &quot;Dragon Lich&quot; with &quot;Necromancy 5&quot;, you'll also be able to create &quot;Adamantium&quot; or &quot;Mithril&quot; with Matter 5, you'll be able to commune with the spirits of the forest with Spirit, and many other &quot;non-necrom-esque&quot; activities.<br /> <br /> I really wish that wasnt the case, but it is. Game mechanics dictates the setting in sense, so they should be built to fit into it rather they just having a label of &quot;ignore those when convenient&quot;.<br /> <br /> Game mechanics are like the &quot;laws of physics&quot; of the real world. We cant say that &quot;gravity is just the game mechanics of our simulation matrix&quot;. If you have broken game mechanics, the setting wont make sense.<br /> <br /> For instance, in the game &quot;Looney tunes&quot;, damage dont really hurts. If you KO an enemy, they spend an amount of rounds seeing starts around their heads, until they recover. That's the game mechanics about setting that is about doing funny stunts and nobody ever gets hurt, even when they are run out by a train.<br /> <br /> Imagine applying those same game mechanics to WoD and saying &quot;it's just game mechanics&quot;. The world wouldnt make sense. </div> </div> </div>Game mechanics are abstractions meant to let us at the gaming table quickly adjudicate results. They are not the physical or metaphysical rules of the world, they are quick hacks to get a very rough approximation of something much more messy and complicated. Because they are meant to approach specific elements they sometimes look a bit like the rules of the world (that's what's happening in your Looney Tunes example), but that's happenstance not physical or metaphysical truth. <br /> <br /> You bring up gravity and that's a perfect example because falling damage rules in games are usually quite rough. Most games either implicitly or explicitly have the same gravity as our world and yet falling damage rules almost never match. You can't extrapolate the force of gravity from them and you'd get quite entertaining results if you tried. The WoD has lethal damage kick in at 100 feet, which Mage directly calls out as not matching our reality.<br /> <br /> In your Looney Tunes example, the rules say the characters see stars for a certain amount of time, but in universe there isn't a rule that specifies how long. That length of time is an abstraction meant to translate the world we are trying to depict into game terms. The rules approach the world, not the other way around. Dr. Sylvester can't study head stars to put together a grand unified theory of concussions unless it is funny. A grand unified theory of concussions doesn't even exist in universe unless it is funny. Funny is the metaphysics of the world, not dice.<br /> <br /> There was an old D&amp;D third edition idea for continental travel by lining up a thousand miles of kobolds and using greater cleave on them. As long as you didn't miss you could travel a thousand miles in a single turn. It matched the rules of the game but it didn't match the rules of the world.<br /> <br /> It's the same with Spheres. They are, first and foremost, a way of translating every type of magic into a single system that can be used at the gaming table. That's going to have bugs and unintended consequences. Sometimes that will result in capabilities that don't make sense in world, like the necromythrilmancer. That doesn't constrain us to change how we think of the in game world because the system is not the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T06:35:24-07:00","id":1516768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516755#post1516755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesnt mean they are automatically lying. I do make the case that it would be an interesting game if they actually were lying, that would make them to be much more of a Cabal of powerful individuals, much more like the ideas from the conspiracy theories about the &quot;Illuminatis&quot; and such. I think it would be highly interesting, but in this case they would just be a bunch of <b>hermetic</b> technomancers, disguising their arcane sorcery with the use of mechanic toys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now that this was clarified, yeah, that could be cool. However, I feel people prefer to have the setting Truth as vague as possible and this way *try* to make everyone right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516755#post1516755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing, every single mage in the world cant possibly be all right at the same time. They could all be wrong thou... But despite the claims of the game, there IS some <b>objective truth</b>, even if we dont know what it is.<br /> <br /> If the Techies are right (I dont think so but ok), the Trads are wrong, and vice versa. Or both could be wrong.<br /> <br /> But MtA aint a solipsistic illusion built for each sole individual.<br /> <br /> (Late for work, answer more later, bye)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not sure about that. About the Purple paradigm, everyone is kinda wrong, but Technomancers are &quot;more wrong&quot;, or further from the truth than mystics. About Avatars, I feel that neither is wrong, as the setting itself does not define Avatars well enough for us to judge who's right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516755#post1516755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you need the &quot;just mechanics that has nothing to do with the setting at all&quot; of the Spheres: Spirit, Matter, Life and maybe also Entropy and Prime.<br /> <br /> Meaning that, besides being able to fuse a pile of bodies into a &quot;Dragon Lich&quot; with &quot;Necromancy 5&quot;, you'll also be able to create &quot;Adamantium&quot; or &quot;Mithril&quot; with Matter 5, you'll be able to commune with the spirits of the forest with Spirit, and many other &quot;non-necrom-esque&quot; activities.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. You are still limited by your paradigm. So, if your necromancer only believes he can mess with the dead and spirits and the like, he might not be able to do any of the things you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T07:51:49-07:00","id":1516780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516768#post1516768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily. You are still limited by your paradigm. So, if your necromancer only believes he can mess with the dead and spirits and the like, he might not be able to do any of the things you said.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a bit weird for some levels thou, upon which there would be no increment, but you'd still have to &quot;learn&quot;.<br /> <br /> I do work with an alternate system of &quot;Realms&quot; from Gurps, so my &quot;Spheres&quot; are custom tailored for each group. That was my work around, total headcanon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T14:15:44-07:00","id":1516915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516780#post1516780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a bit weird for some levels thou, upon which there would be no increment, but you'd still have to &quot;learn&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The \u201cnecromancy only\u201d mage is a fairly extreme example; but the idea that Lord Revan is describing is actually how the developers prefer to handle the issue: if the Sphere system says that you have enough dots to say that you can do something, but it's not something that your Focus permits you to do, then you can't do it.<br /> <br /> Mostly. There's always the fallback to \u201cWorking Without Focus\u201d which adds a Willpower expenditure and greatly increases the difficulty of the Working (+3); and in this way, a non-technomancer can brute-force an Effect that he doesn't believe in through sheer force of will. (Non-technomancers can also discard Instruments ahead of schedule, which isn't nearly as rough as Working Without Focus \u2014 +1 difficulty and no Willpower cost \u2014 but the principle is the same; so I tend to lump these together.)<br /> <br /> But aside from Working Without Focus, if your Focus can't justify you doing something, you can't do it. Even if you have the Spheres you need to do it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516780#post1516780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do work with an alternate system of &quot;Realms&quot; from Gurps, so my &quot;Spheres&quot; are custom tailored for each group. That was my work around, total headcanon</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're not already familiar with the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/388362\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Fragments</a>, I would strongly recommend picking it up. It's a STV product, so it lacks official backing; but if you're willing to accept head-canon workarounds, it's a pretty good one. <br /> <br /> Another one I like is the idea to partially decouple Rotes from Spheres: that is, make it so that someone who doesn't have the Spheres necessary to perform an Effect can still do so if they have access to an appropriate Rote. Spheres then become a measure of your ability to improvise Magick, representing an understanding of its principles to a level beyond mere book learning to the point where you just intuitively <i>get it</i> and making you a virtuoso with it.<br /> <br /> Independently learnable Rotes, meanwhile, would let you pick up one or two (or three or four, etc) neat tricks, rounding out your options and letting a mage do things that his Focus says he ought to be able to do, but which his Sphere dots don't permit. The downside being that with things the mage knows <i>only</i> by Rote, he lacks the ability to improvise. He <i>cannot</i> Work Without Focus or grow beyond Instruments when performing by Rote; and his ability to vary the formula to do something similar but not the same is limited. <br /> <br /> And, of course, once you have the Spheres needed to perform the Effect, the Rote ceases to be all that important. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T19:44:39-07:00","id":1517131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516915#post1516915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly. There's always the fallback to \u201cWorking Without Focus\u201d which adds a Willpower expenditure and greatly increases the difficulty of the Working (+3); and in this way, a non-technomancer can brute-force an Effect that he doesn't believe in through sheer force of will. (Non-technomancers can also discard Instruments ahead of schedule, which isn't nearly as rough as Working Without Focus \u2014 +1 difficulty and no Willpower cost \u2014 but the principle is the same; so I tend to lump these together.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about that. It's working without instruments, not working without focus. If your paradigm don't allow it, I'd say you can't do it. Or at least have to find some logic into it working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T21:26:57-07:00","id":1517134,"title":"","content":"M20 pp.566\u2013567:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Working Without Focus</b><br /> <br /> Because mages are vessels of Will, they can sometimes will things to happen without using tools or a practice. Working through determination alone, a mage Cancer pass or focus and conjure effects without channeling belief through practice or tools.<br /> <br /> Working this way doesn't happen without cost. Game wise, the player spends one willpower point and suffers a plus three difficulty to his roll. Essentially, that Mage throws every ounce of self-conviction he has into the spell, using will alone to focus his intents.</div><br /> As well, the Magical Modifiers lists \u201cworking without instruments\u201d as a +3 difficulty, but make no mention of requiring a Willpower expenditure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T22:38:31-07:00","id":1517139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1516755#post1516755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That doesnt mean they are automatically lying. I do make the case that it would be an interesting game if they actually were lying, that would make them to be much more of a Cabal of powerful individuals, much more like the ideas from the conspiracy theories about the &quot;Illuminatis&quot; and such. I think it would be highly interesting, but in this case they would just be a bunch of <b>hermetic</b> technomancers, disguising their arcane sorcery with the use of mechanic toys.<br /> <br /> That would be an interesting game, but very different from MtA.<br /> <br /> In fact, Gurps has this exact game: <b>The Cabal</b>. It's a cool one too, and much much more &quot;paranoid conspiracy theory&quot; than MtA.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the game you're describing is mage the ascension 1st edition, where technocrats knows that they're doing magic and use technology as merely a tool for their arcane goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T07:30:59-07:00","id":1517158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1517134#post1517134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 pp.566\u2013567:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Working Without Focus</b><br /> <br /> Because mages are vessels of Will, they can sometimes will things to happen without using tools or a practice. Working through determination alone, a mage Cancer pass or focus and conjure effects without channeling belief through practice or tools.<br /> <br /> Working this way doesn't happen without cost. Game wise, the player spends one willpower point and suffers a plus three difficulty to his roll. Essentially, that Mage throws every ounce of self-conviction he has into the spell, using will alone to focus his intents.</div><br /> As well, the Magical Modifiers lists \u201cworking without instruments\u201d as a +3 difficulty, but make no mention of requiring a Willpower expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it wouldn't be the first time sections did not match up, though it could also be the difference between working without instruments and working without a practice.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T19:25:03-07:00","id":1517188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1515686-safety-vs-freedom?p=1517134#post1517134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 pp.566\u2013567:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Working Without Focus</b><br /> <br /> Because mages are vessels of Will, they can sometimes will things to happen without using tools or a practice. Working through determination alone, a mage Cancer pass or focus and conjure effects without channeling belief through practice or tools.<br /> <br /> Working this way doesn't happen without cost. Game wise, the player spends one willpower point and suffers a plus three difficulty to his roll. Essentially, that Mage throws every ounce of self-conviction he has into the spell, using will alone to focus his intents.</div><br /> As well, the Magical Modifiers lists \u201cworking without instruments\u201d as a +3 difficulty, but make no mention of requiring a Willpower expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that they never used the word focus. But practices and instruments. So, you don't seem to be able to ditch Paradigm. Then as long as it fits your paradigm, you can do it without practices and instruments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}